    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15153": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant Electrical Engineering (ECE) AY26-27",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant Electrical Engineering (ECE) AY26-27 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant Electrical Engineering (ECE) AY26-27 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply on line; attach an up-to-date resume; attach undergraduate and graduate transcripts (unofficial ones are acceptable) Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant Electrical Engineering (ECE) AY26-27 Posting Number AS1166P Subdivision School of Engineering and Computing Division Col. of Engineering & Business Department Electrical & Cyber Engineering Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The ECE department is soliciting applications for a Graduate Assistant position in the fields of electrical engineering. This GA will support ECE’s efforts to improve ECE’s outreach & recruitment capabilities, and outcomes of outreach & recruitment activities. Duties will include, but not be limited to, assist in developing technology-based outreach platforms and preparing & conducting outreach activities under ECE chairperson’s supervision. This appointment is for an academic year (fall and spring) but continuation in 27/SP will be subject to performance evaluation in the end of 26/FA semester. Career Readiness Learning Objectives ( NACE ) Communication – Be able to clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives with the faculty supervisor and any others working on the assigned project. Critical Thinking – Be able to identify technical issues, as applicable, arising from project activities and come up with feasible approaches to addressing those issues. Dissemination of Results Present the outcomes of your experience at Celebrate Gannon and/or other venues determined by the college. Required Qualifications - Good communication and teamwork skills - Hands-on and working knowledge for the work in laboratory settings, utilizing electronic devices, software tools, and Windows and Linux operating systems - Quick learner; be able to deliver Preferred Qualifications - Strong background in electrical and computer engineering. - Hands-on experience in computer networking - Proficiency and hand-on experience in Linux operating systems Physical Demands Typical physical work in ECE lab settings and applicable field testing and/or operation Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Research, Teaching, Athletic Training) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Lab Hours - Depending on mutually-agreed schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Transcripts Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
