    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15215": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Information and Event Services Assistant 26-27",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Information and Event Services Assistant 26-27 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Information and Event Services Assistant 26-27 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please apply before 9/01/26 Position Details Position Summary Position Title Information and Event Services Assistant 26-27 Posting Number Division Student Develpmt&Engagmt VP's Offc Department Student Development & Engagemt Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Career Readiness Learning Objectives Career & Self Development: Gain valuable experience that will prepare you for future professional roles in customer service, event management, and other fields. Develop a deeper understanding of the operations and services within a campus environment. Enhance your resume with practical skills and experiences that are highly valued by employers. Communication: Improve communication skills by providing clear and accurate information to customers in person, over the phone, and via email. Enhance the ability to convey information effectively, ensuring customers understand directions, event details, and services offered. Critical Thinking: Develop the ability to analyze and address customer inquiries and issues efficiently. Enhance problem-solving skills by troubleshooting AV equipment and resolving technical issues during events. Cultivate the capacity to think on your feet and make quick, informed decisions in a dynamic environment. Equity & Inclusion: Improve intercultural competency by interacting with a diverse range of students, staff, and visitors. Develop the ability to communicate effectively and respectfully with individuals from various cultural backgrounds. Enhance your understanding and appreciation of different perspectives and cultural practices. Leadership: Build leadership skills by taking initiative in setting up event spaces and ensuring everything is ready for events. Develop the ability to lead by example, maintaining a professional demeanor and providing excellent customer service. Enhance your capacity to manage responsibilities independently while supporting the team and guiding customers. Professionalism: Cultivate a strong work ethic by managing multiple responsibilities, including customer service, event support, and information desk duties. Develop a sense of accountability and reliability, ensuring tasks are completed accurately and on time. Enhance professionalism through consistent, courteous interactions with customers and colleagues. Teamwork: Foster teamwork by working closely with other staff members and event organizers to ensure smooth event execution. Develop collaboration skills through coordinating with supervisors and colleagues on various tasks and projects. Enhance the ability to work as part of a team, contributing to a positive and productive work environment. Technology: Gain hands-on experience with AV equipment, improving technical skills and digital literacy. Develop the ability to set up, operate, and troubleshoot audio-visual systems for events. Enhance proficiency with digital communication tools and office software used for event planning and customer service. SUMMARY The Information Desk and Event Services Assistant is a vital member of the Leadership Development and Campus Engagement team, responsible for providing excellent customer service and event support. This role includes staffing the information desk, assisting customers with inquiries, and supporting events by setting up event spaces and providing AV tech support within the Waldron Campus Center complex. The Information Desk and Event Services Assistant plays a key role in ensuring a positive experience for visitors and the smooth execution of events in the Waldron Campus Center complex. If you are enthusiastic about providing exceptional service and enjoy a variety of responsibilities, we encourage you to apply. RESPONSIBILITIES Information Desk Support: Greet visitors, students, and staff with a friendly and professional demeanor, providing immediate assistance and directing individuals to the appropriate services or locations. Provide clear and accurate information about campus services, events, and locations, maintaining a thorough knowledge of campus maps, departmental services, and contact information. Respond to phone calls and emails promptly and courteously, handling questions, and providing solutions to common inquiries regarding campus events, services, and facilities. Keep the information desk area clean, organized, and stocked with necessary materials, such as brochures, maps, etc. for distribution for interested individuals. Update bulletin boards and digital displays with current information and announcements to keep the campus community informed. Listen to and address customer needs and concerns in a helpful and efficient manner, following up on requests to ensure satisfaction and resolution. Monitor public areas near the information desk to ensure they are clean, orderly, and welcoming. Report any maintenance or safety issues to the appropriate personnel and assist with special projects or tasks as assigned by supervisors. Monitor activity throughout the building and surrounding areas; enforce building/University guidelines (no smoking; shoes & shirts; no animals, etc.) as needed. Report problems to supervisor as needed. Collaborate with other staff members will be essential to ensure comprehensive support for campus events and services. Assist with special tasks such as equipment inventory, office furniture moving, delivery load in/out, etc. as assigned. Event Support: Assist in setting up event spaces by arranging furniture and equipment according to event specifications, ensuring the spaces are clean and properly configured before events begin. Set up and test audio-visual equipment prior to events, troubleshooting and resolving any technical issues that arise. Working closely with event planners to understand and meet their specific needs, you will provide on-site support during events to ensure smooth execution. Be present at the event to provide immediate support when necessary. After events conclude, you will ensure event spaces are returned to their original condition and store equipment and furniture appropriately. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS Ability to move furniture, lift heavy objects, and bend/kneel/stoop as needed; ability to safely and independently lift up to 50 pounds; Strong customer service skills with enthusiasm and ability to work as a team player; Ability to communicate effectively with the public and provide high-quality customer service; Extensive knowledge of the university and surrounding area; Prior use and knowledge of personal computers, software, and AV/media equipment is strongly preferred; Ability to work independently and take initiative; Be enrolled as a full-time student at Gannon University and maintain a cumulative GPA of at least 2.5. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in a customer service or event support role is preferred. Familiarity with the Waldron Campus Center and its services will be beneficial. Physical Demands This position may require evening and weekend hours to support events. Physical ability to set up event spaces, including moving furniture and equipment, is necessary. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 5 Job Posting Open Date 08/01/2026 Job Posting Close Date 10/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please apply before 9/01/26 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please list your daily availability, in this format:\r\nDay | Available from | Available to (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to work weekends? Yes No * Briefly describe any customer service experience you may have. (Open Ended Question) * Are you willing and able to do work that requires standing, walking, and/or heavy lifting when needed? yes no Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14862": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | RWC Building Attendant - Academic Year 26-27 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help RWC Building Attendant - Academic Year 26-27 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please contact the RWC with any questions regarding this job. Position Details Position Summary Position Title RWC Building Attendant - Academic Year 26-27 Posting Number Division Recreation & Wellness Department Student Development & Engagemt Location Erie, Pa Position Summary POSITION SUMMARY : Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Communication: Clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives between co-workers and shifts to ensure jobs are done properly and effectively. Teamwork: Build and maintain collaborative relationships to work effectively toward common goals, and ensure everyone in the workplace feels they are treated equally and as part of a team. Professionalism: Knowing work environments differ greatly, understand and demonstrate effective work habits, and act in interest of the RWC , its workers and the community members. Responsibilities: Building Attendants are responsible for overseeing specific areas within the Recreation and Wellness Center, the upkeep and cleanliness of the equipment and surroundings, answering questions and assisting patrons as needed, and to assist the Building Supervisor in enacting safety protocols when required. Attendants need to be knowledgeable on the facility and its amenities and must be able to communicate effectively with all patrons. Attendants are responsible for a variety of Front Desk operations including: checking in/out equipment, handling various sales (everything except for memberships and locker rentals), answering the telephone, enforcing the policies and procedures of Gannon University and the Recreation and Wellness Center, and any additional tasks that may be assigned. Building Attendants are expected to be educated on other campus programs and events that may take place in the facility and/or around campus. This position requires high quality customer service, demonstration of leadership skills, adaptability and quick-thinking skills, the ability to take direction and be a team player. Average Hours: 8-12 hours/week ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : 1. Oversee dedicated area (cardio deck or weight room) at designated podium. 2. Responsible for completing assigned tasks from Building Supervisor on duty. 3. Handle other assigned duties or special projects as assigned by the professional staff and/or building supervisor 4. Work special events that may take place on evenings, weekends, campus breaks, and across campus. 5. Monitor quality of equipment and report damage to Building Supervisor on duty. 6. Maintain cleanliness and organization of ALL equipment and sanitize equipment and podiums. 7. Assist as a spotter for patrons as needed and provide information on equipment upon request. 8. Assist in emergencies and first aid as necessary. 9. Required to attend all mandatory staff meeting and staff trainings. 10. Complete mandatory student development and engagement credits per semester. 11. Knowledgeable of all Gannon University and Recreation and Wellness Center policies. Must enforce and apply all policies and procedures during scheduled shift. 12. Provide a professional, welcoming, and inclusive environment for all who enter the facility. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS : Education: Enrolled full-time student of Gannon University preferably with a minimum of a 2.5 GPA Experience: Experience must include use of Microsoft Word, Excel, and use of standard office equipment such as copy machine, printer, and telephone. Previous customer service, recreation, or fitness experience preferred. Certifications: Certified in CPR & AED *Training offered upon hire Skills: Leadership skills including strong verbal and written communication skills, working in a team atmosphere, and professionalism. Individual must be able to work with a diverse population that would include students, faculty, staff, alumni and community members. Must be able to work independently without direct supervision on day to day tasks and be able to take initiative. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS : Ability to lift and carry weight, possibly up to 50lbs unassisted Ability to walk, stand, and move about for approximately 2-8 hours; without access to a chair Ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl Ability to climb (stairs/ladders) or balance Ability to walk around building and potentially across campus Repetitive movement of hands, arms and legs, such as sweeping, vacuuming, and moping Meet the physical demands associated with a busy office and University environment. WORKING CONDITIONS : Work is performed in a busy campus-wide setting. Some evening and weekend hours are required for activities and events which require representation from members of the Student Development and Engagement Office. Must be a team player, willing to cover or trade shifts when necessary. Must be available to work days, evenings, weekends, and campus holiday breaks as necessary. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 50 Job Posting Open Date 08/07/2026 Job Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Please contact the RWC with any questions regarding this job. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you eligible for Federal Work Study as determined by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Unsure * What would be your most significant contribution or positive aspect that you would bring to our program? (Open Ended Question) * List all experiences with Recreation and Wellness Center programs and activities you have taken a part of (group fitness classes, intramural sports, sport clubs, special events, etc.) (Open Ended Question) * What is your current cumulative GPA?  If your GPA drops below a 2.5 would you be willing to participate in a Study Hall and possibly be temporarily suspended from working until grades improve? (Open Ended Question) * Is there anything that may interfere with your work availability at the Recreation and Wellness Center (other jobs, internships, observations, meeting, clubs, etc.)? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently certified in American Red Cross CPR/AED?  If so, when do they expire?  If not, do you agree to get certified before starting work?  Will you need training from the RWC? (Open Ended Question) * Are you able and willing to do heavy lifting and moving when the job requires it? yes no * Are you available to work nights? Yes No * Are you available to work weekends? Yes No * Feel free to list any additional comments that you feel would help us in placing you in a staff position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
