    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15031": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Assessment and Program Support Graduate Assistant, Dahlkemper School of Business",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assessment and Program Support Graduate Assistant, Dahlkemper School of Business Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assessment and Program Support Graduate Assistant, Dahlkemper School of Business Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assessment and Program Support Graduate Assistant, Dahlkemper School of Business Posting Number AS1115P Subdivision School of Business Division Col. of Engineering & Business Department Master of Business Admin Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Gannon University’s Dahlkemper School of Business ( DSB ) is currently seeking a Graduate Assistant for the Fall 2026/Spring 2027 semesters. Applicants must be an admitted graduate student who is actively pursuing their degree full time. This position includes remitted tuition benefits and a stipend. The work schedule is typically 10 hours per week. The appointment is for one year. Graduate Assistant reports to the Program Directors of the MBA -BA and Online MBA and are a part of a team including a Program Assistant and student employees who contribute assistance with the day-to-day work of the Business School. Job Description: Marketing Efforts Organizing on-campus professional events (i.e., Speaker Series) Social media responsibilities, including student highlights DSB Support Activities Retention and recruitment activities for DSB Working with other students to assist them in University processes Covering classes for undergraduate faculty members and/or administering undergraduate exams when necessary Supporting faculty research and activities Program Research Conducting curriculum research for DSB programs Researching information for program changes Analyzing current program assessment data Office Management Offering support for and filling in for DSB Program Assistant. Performing additional duties in all areas as assigned by the CEB Dean’s Office, MBA Program Directors, DSB Chairs, DSB Program Assistant, or other leadership NACE Competencies: Critical Thinking: Multi-task well in a fast-paced autonomous environment. Professionalism: Prioritize and complete tasks to accomplish organizational goals. Required Qualifications Applicants must be an admitted graduate student who is actively pursuing their degree full time. Preferred Qualifications Former DSB 4+1 student. Physical Demands Ability to work 10-hours per week in an office setting Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Support Office Position Type GA (Lab Assistant/Tutoring) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 8M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule 10-hours per week Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
