    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15195": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | VR Graduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Gannon University  | VR Graduate Research Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help VR Graduate Research Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit via PeopleAdmin: 1. Resume 2. Transcripts (undergraduate and graduate, if applicable) 3. Cover letter (optional, recommended) Interested candidates should apply by Sunday, August 30, 2026 . For more information contact: Dr. Jinhee Yoo (Professor of Sport Business, Principal Investigator) E-mail: yoo002@gannon.edu Phone: (814) 871-7586 Position Details Posting Summary Position Title VR Graduate Research Assistant Posting Number AS1095P Subdivision School of Business Division Col. of Engineering & Business Department Management Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Career Readiness Learning Objectives 1. Communication: The Research Assistant will clearly and effectively communicate with (1) Dr. Jinhee Yoo (Principal Investigator, PI) and (2) participants for recruiting, coordinating the experiment sessions, and executing research experiments. 2. Professionalism: The Research Assistant will understand and respect the confidentiality of the research participants as they will have access to the participants’ personal information. Practicing confidentiality is a key part of professionalism. The Research Assistant will also demonstrate punctuality and respect for both PI and participants. Purpose The primary responsibility of the Graduate Research Assistant is to work directly with Dr. Yoo regarding her research projects on virtual reality (VR) gaming, sport consumer behavior, online consumer behavior, etc. The Research Assistant will be responsible for assisting the PI in a variety of non-administrative tasks in support of the research activities which may include but not be limited to (1) preparing resources, equipment, and materials for the research, (2) recruiting research participants, (3) executing research experiments and data collection, (4) documenting results, etc. Required Qualifications Must be a Gannon University graduate student enrolled for both the Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters, and available to work throughout the entire 2026/2027 academic year. Graduate students in Business, Psychology, Communications, Engineering, or related field only. GPA of 3.0 or higher at both the undergraduate and graduate levels Proficient in using Excel Excellent verbal and written communication skills Preferred Qualifications Looking for a responsible, professional, proactive, and detail-oriented candidate who is flexible and adaptable to meet the demands of the research schedule. Candidates with strong sales experience or demonstrated outreach and engagement skills are preferred. Physical Demands Should not have any limitations using VR headsets (i.e., no history of seizure or epilepsy). Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Research, Teaching, Athletic Training) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Data Collection Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Transcripts Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15158": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Writing &amp; Research Center Consultant I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Writing & Research Center Consultant I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. REQUIRED: Writing Sample and 2 recommendations send via email to Elizabeth Kons (kons001@gannon.edu) Position Details Position Summary Position Title Writing & Research Center Consultant I Posting Number Division Library Department Provost & Student Experience (AA) Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Critical Thinking/Problem Solving : Evaluate complex writing issues and develop solutions. Use sound reasoning to analyze a student’s work and provide constructive feedback. Oral/Written Communications : Provide clear, concise, and organized verbal feedback. Write detailed commentary on student papers. Convey complex writing principles in understandable terms. Teamwork/Collaboration : Work harmoniously with other tutors to share strategies and insights. Collaborate with faculty and staff to ensure consistent tutoring methodologies. Understand and respect diverse writing styles and perspectives. Digital Technology : Efficiently use digital platforms and tools (like grammar checkers, online databases) to assist in tutoring. Stay updated with the latest digital resources and platforms used in writing research and tutoring. Leadership : Take the initiative in guiding students through the writing process. Demonstrate the ability to influence and guide student writers without dominating their original voice. Participate in tutor training and development sessions, sometimes leading them. Professionalism/Work Ethic : Exhibit punctuality, dependability, and preparedness for each tutoring session. Uphold the writing center’s standards, ethics, and confidentiality guidelines. Demonstrate patience and resilience with challenging tutoring scenarios. Global/Intercultural Fluency : Respectfully engage with writers from diverse cultural, linguistic, and educational backgrounds. Recognize and value diverse perspectives in writing and communication. Equity and Inclusion : Understand and respect the unique voices, experiences, and backgrounds of all students. Adopt strategies to ensure inclusivity in tutoring sessions, making sure every student feels valued and understood. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide one-to-one writing consultations with undergraduate students, focusing on improving their writing skills. Mentor students by providing guidance and feedback on their writing and helping them develop effective writing strategies. Open and close the Writing Center, ensuring that all equipment and materials are properly stored and secured. Maintain the center’s schedule, coordinating appointments and walk-ins with available writing consultants. Answer emails and inquiries from students and faculty, providing information about the services offered by the center and how to access them. Conduct workshops and presentations as necessary to help students improve their writing skills, including topics such as thesis statements, organization, and citation styles. Maintain accurate records of student consultations. Required Qualifications Must be a student at Gannon University enrolled full time, with a minimum 3.6 GPA Strong writing skills and a deep understanding of the writing process, including academic writing conventions and citation styles. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with students and faculty. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities. Ability to work independently and as part of a team of writing consultants. Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to provide constructive feedback. Familiarity with academic writing conventions and citation styles. Flexibility and adaptability, with the ability to respond to changing priorities and demands. Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion, and the ability to work effectively with a diverse student population. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands n/a Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 4 Job Posting Open Date 08/26/2026 Job Posting Close Date 05/07/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants REQUIRED : Writing Sample and 2 recommendations send via email to Elizabeth Kons (kons001@gannon.edu) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires constant communicating, both in person and electronically.  Are you fluent in English? yes no * What is your current cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience tutoring writing? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Transcripts Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15097": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | STEM Center - Tutor - Major: Mech Eng Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help STEM Center - Tutor - Major: Mech Eng Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Position Details Position Summary Position Title STEM Center - Tutor - Major: Mech Eng Posting Number Division Library Department Provost & Student Experience (AA) Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Believe in your own knowledge and perseverance, and the amazing potential of Gannon students Lead Gannon students to conquer their academic hurdles, both small and large Unleash your love for your major and your favorite courses Enjoy making a deep impact on a very flexible schedule Key responsibilities and highlights: Tutor peers in STEM subject material they are qualified to cover May seek or perform other necessary STEM Center work, with approval Some initial and ongoing (paid) training is likely to be required Position structure: Will have one regular paid guaranteed shift per week (likely 3 hours, and in the late afternoon and early evening such as 4-7PM on a Sunday-Thursday); work during this shift will be tutoring, preparation/training, other tasks to support the STEM Center and our stakeholders, or other work to benefit the University Needs to establish additional availability within library hours of operation for “on-call” tutoring (paid for actual tutoring appointments only; up to ~3 additional hours if holding appointments, more may be possible but cannot be guaranteed) There will basically be one such tutor per major (one per set of similar majors) for each area traditionally served by the STEM Center Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Critical Thinking/Problem Solving: A STEM tutor can develop critical thinking and problem-solving skills by breaking down complex concepts for students, identifying gaps in their understanding, and helping them develop strategies to solve problems. Oral/Written Communication: STEM tutors need to clearly explain complex ideas and concepts to students within tutoring sessions and in interactions with coworkers and STEM Center management. Tutors may be required to speak to classes, reach out to students, and represent the STEM Center at functions or events. Additionally, tutors may be required to send emails, make phone calls, or initiate other communication on behalf of the STEM Center. Teamwork/Collaboration: STEM tutors can facilitate or assist with group study sessions and participate in other projects or initiatives to support the STEM Center. Digital Technology: Tutors may create online resources, utilizing software or apps to visualize concepts, and must make extensive use of scheduling systems, MS Teams, and other software to perform essential functions of the job. Leadership: In working with a variety of students, tutors have regular opportunity to thrive in changing environments, to identify and address complex problems, and to navigate ambiguity. Professionalism/Work Ethic: By being punctual, prepared, and professional in their interactions with students, tutors can showcase a strong work ethic. They must also adhere to ethical guidelines and respect the confidentiality of their students. Career Management: The STEM Center is a cocurricular opportunity to develop and showcase the ability to build success in others and specifically to teach or train others. Tutoring course material often builds additional competencies in those areas. Global/Intercultural Fluency: To develop global and intercultural fluency, tutors often have opportunities to work with a diverse slate of Gannon students, learning, understanding, and adapting to academic and nonacademic facets of culture and communication. Required Qualifications Major and significant course load matching position title High GPA and positive reputation with faculty Interpersonal excellence Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands N/A Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Job Posting Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Have you or will you soon complete the REQUIRED questionnaire at: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV ? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
