    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15217": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Applied Exercise Science Graduate Assistant (Teaching and Research) Morosky School of Health Professions and Sciences",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Applied Exercise Science Graduate Assistant (Teaching and Research) Morosky School of Health Professions and Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Applied Exercise Science Graduate Assistant (Teaching and Research) Morosky School of Health Professions and Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Applied Exercise Science Graduate Assistant (Teaching and Research) Morosky School of Health Professions and Sciences Posting Number AS1163P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Applied Exercise Science Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Graduate Assistants in the Applied Exercise Science Graduate Program will be required to: 1. Teach lab courses pertaining to Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology, Exercise Testing & Prescription, and Care & Prevention of Athletic Injuries 2. Assist in lab practical testing situations. 3. Conduct open lab hours for undergraduate students. 4. Help lead and conduct exercise testing on student-athletes and community members in the Human Performance Lab ( HPL ). 5. Assist faculty in the Applied Exercise Science department with new and ongoing research projects. 6. Assist faculty in departmental administrative duties. Required Qualifications Applicants for the Applied Exercise Science Graduate Assistant position should possess the following qualifications: 1. Current graduate student in the Masters of Sport & Exercise Science ( MSES ) program. 2. Familiarity with lab equipment used in exercise testing. 3. Comfortable with public speaking. 4. Capacity to communicate ideas and techniques to different groups. 5. Willingness to work closely with department faculty. Preferred Qualifications N/A Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical and technical demands of busy office, classroom, and laboratory settings established for teaching and research within the discipline of exercise science. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Research, Teaching, Athletic Training) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
