    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15199": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant (Master of Healthcare Administration)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant (Master of Healthcare Administration) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant (Master of Healthcare Administration) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Gannon University’s Master of Healthcare Administration program is currently seeking a Graduate Assistant for the Fall 2026/Spring 2027 semesters. Applicant must be an admitted graduate student who is actively pursuing their degree full-time . Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant (Master of Healthcare Administration) Posting Number AS1136P Subdivision School of Business Division Col. of Engineering & Business Department Master of Healthcare Administration Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Faculty Support Activities Support remote faculty with hybrid technology for face-to-face classes. Requires availability up to 3 hours once a week, according to course schedule. Must be familiar with MS Teams. Support faculty course/curriculum updates in the university’s Learning Management System. Must be familiar with Blackboard. Support faculty in developing PowerPoint material for classroom activities. Must be familiar with PowerPoint. Support faculty in grading assignments in Blackboard, as needed. Program Support Activities Provide analytical support for program metrics, such as student and alumni data as well as survey analysis. Must be familiar with Excel. Provide report-writing and data-gathering support according to accreditation requirements. Office Management Provide support for other faculty in the Dahlkemper School of Business when requested, such as occasional proctoring of exams. NACE Competencies: Critical Thinking: Multitask well in a fast-paced autonomous environment. Professionalism: Prioritize and complete tasks to accomplish organizational goals. This position includes remitted tuition benefits and a stipend. The work schedule is typically 10 hours per week. The appointment is for one year. The Graduate Assistant reports to the MHA Program Director. Required Qualifications Admitted full-time graduate student, preferably in the MHA . Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with Excel, PowerPoint and Blackboard. Physical Demands Ability to work in an office and school environment 10 hours/week. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Support Office Position Type GA (Lab Assistant/Tutoring) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 8M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule M-F Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
