    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14768": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Assistant Coach, Competitive Cheer",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assistant Coach, Competitive Cheer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Coach, Competitive Cheer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Coach, Competitive Cheer Posting Number AS1139P Subdivision Athletic Director's Office Division Athletics Department Competitive Cheer and Stunt Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Assistant Competitive Cheer Coach Coach position is a part-time, 10-month position responsible for assisting the Head Coach in all aspects of the Gannon University Competitive Cheer & Dance program. The program competes at the intercollegiate II level and attends the NCA & NDA Collegiate National Championship annually. Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : 1. Recruits quality academic students who are also competitive student-athletes. 2. Trains, strengthens, and develops all cheer and/or dance student-athletes, under the direction of the Head Coach. 3. Learns, understands, and complies with all USA Cheer rules (cheer), NDA safety rules (dance) and Gannon University regulations. 4. Promotes and represents the University whenever possible. 5. Assists in the development and implementation of a year-round strength and conditioning program for the team. 6. Assists with administrative tasks related to the Competitive Cheer & Dance program as requested by the Head Coach. 7. Assists in the development and implementation of camps and clinics. 8. Teaches advanced level stunting, baskets, and pyramids safely and with proper technique. 9. Teaches and spots beginner to elite tumbling skills safely and with proper technique. 10. Performs other duties as assigned within the scope and responsibility and requirements of the job. Required Qualifications Education: A bachelor’s degree; working knowledge of USA Cheer and/or NDA safety rules and an understanding of the philosophy behind them. Licensure: A valid driver’s license with a good driving history is required. Skills: Must have excellent communication skills and technical knowledge of the sport-specific skills identified above for cheer or dance, combined with the ability to effectively teach and coach them. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Experience: Cheer or dance experience at the collegiate level; preferably with competitive experience at NCA & NDA Nationals. Team coaching experience at the high school level or higher. Experience participating on or coaching programs that have a collaborative approach to their cheer and dance programs. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy athletic team schedule. Work is performed indoors and outdoors in a busy University setting. The work schedule will vary. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 10M Hours per Week As required. Work Schedule Flexible work schedule required. Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
