    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15050": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant (Tutoring and Lab Assistants); 1st year Anatomy-FA 26",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant (Tutoring and Lab Assistants); 1st year Anatomy-FA 26 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant (Tutoring and Lab Assistants); 1st year Anatomy-FA 26 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant (Tutoring and Lab Assistants); 1st year Anatomy-FA 26 Posting Number AS1156P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Physical Therapy Program Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Doctor of Physical Therapy Program at Gannon University is committed to excellence in student-centered learning, with an emphasis on student learning outcomes. Graduate Assistants play an important role in achieving these outcomes by working collaboratively with program faculty and fellow Graduate Assistants to support program operations, facilitate open laboratory experiences, provide academic support as requested by faculty, and assist with clinical practice opportunities. While each Graduate Assistant has primary responsibilities, all GAs are expected to work collaboratively, support one another, and contribute to program needs as they arise. As leaders and representatives of the DPT Program, Graduate Assistants are expected to demonstrate professionalism, initiative, flexibility, maintain student confidentiality, and conduct themselves in a manner that reflects the standards and values of the program. This position is for students beginning the first year of the DPT program. Career Readiness Competencies Communication: Effectively communicate with faculty, peers, and students while demonstrating respect for diverse learning styles, communication abilities, and cultural backgrounds. Teamwork: Collaborate with faculty and fellow Graduate Assistants to support program operations, assist one another as needed, and contribute to shared program goals. Professionalism: Demonstrate initiative, flexibility, dependability, confidentiality, and timely completion of responsibilities while serving as a leader and representative of the DPT Program. Responsibilities in the fall semester: 1. Ensure that all students follow laboratory safety guidelines, wear appropriate attire, including long pants, closed-toed shoes, and eye protection, and maintain professional conduct during scheduled laboratory times. 2. Complete cadaver dissections according to provided instructions. 3. Coordinate open laboratory sessions for first-year anatomy students and ensure adherence to laboratory safety expectations. 4. Assist with maintaining an inventory of essential laboratory materials, including nitrile gloves and dissection kits. 5. Ensure that all laboratory surfaces and tools are properly cleaned and disinfected following dissections and open laboratory sessions. 6. Assist faculty with administrative tasks and other responsibilities as assigned. Responsibilities in the spring semester 1. Assist with maintaining physical therapy laboratory environments, including organization, laboratory set-up and clean-up, inventory, and laundry. 2. Assist faculty with administrative tasks and other responsibilities as assigned. Required Qualifications Enrollment as a first-year student in the Gannon University Doctor of Physical Therapy Program. Successful completion of cadaver-based anatomy course Demonstrate professionalism, dependability, and organizational skills. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Ability to work collaboratively as part of the Graduate Assistant team and contribute to shared program responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications No instances of academic or professional behavior probation. Physical Demands Fall Semester: Work is performed primarily in the human gross anatomy laboratory. Responsibilities require standing for extended periods, performing fine motor tasks associated with cadaver dissection, and adhering to laboratory safety protocols, including the use of required personal protective equipment. Graduate Assistants must be comfortable working in a cadaver laboratory and around chemical preservatives. Spring Semester: Work is performed primarily in physical therapy teaching laboratories, classrooms, and office settings. Responsibilities require standing for extended periods, assisting with routine laboratory set-up and organization, and using standard instructional and office equipment. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Lab Assistant/Tutoring) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14896": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Faculty (Teaching or Tenure Track) - Villa Maria School of Nursing",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Faculty (Teaching or Tenure Track) - Villa Maria School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Faculty (Teaching or Tenure Track) - Villa Maria School of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Faculty (Teaching or Tenure Track) - Villa Maria School of Nursing Posting Number F254P Division School of Health Professions Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Gannon University is committed to excellence in student-centered learning with an emphasis on student-learning outcomes. The faculty work collaboratively with colleagues; deliver instruction; advise students; engage in scholarly activities in keeping with the Boyer Model of Scholarship as is appropriate to the application and receipt of tenure and promotion at Gannon; and engage in professional, University, and community service activities. All faculty must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its liberal arts and professional education traditions. The Villa Maria School of Nursing currently has one 9-month faculty position available which will be responsible for teaching in both the undergraduate and the graduate programs and clinical education, as assigned. Candidates must provide evidence of competence in diverse teaching methods and effective classroom and clinical instruction. Required Qualifications Must be a registered nurse with a master’s degree in nursing. Must possess or be eligible to obtain nursing licensure in Pennsylvania. Must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its liberal arts and professional education traditions. Preferred Qualifications An earned doctorate in nursing or a closely related field; applicants who are enrolled or in the process of enrolling to doctoral programs are also encouraged to apply. Recent clinical and teaching experience in a program of higher education. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy academic and clinical environment. Tenure Status Tenure Track Position Type Regular Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 9M Credits Per Year 24  (tenure track) or 27 (teaching track) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Resume Transcripts Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
