      "description": "Gannon University  | Gannon University Graduate Research Assistantship in Criminal Justice Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Gannon University Graduate Research Assistantship in Criminal Justice Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Gannon University Graduate Research Assistantship in Criminal Justice Program Posting Number AS1117P Subdivision Dept. Justice Studies and Human Services Division Col.Humanities,Ed.&SocScience Department Criminal Justice Program Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Graduate Research Assistant will support Dr. Magno’s intensive GIS (Geographic Information System) research, focusing on projects in the Philippines and Erie, Pennsylvania. The role requires a willingness to engage in fieldwork, learn GIS software, and have basic knowledge of data management. Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Critical Thinking: The research assistant will aid in fieldwork data collection and help to analyze patterns seen in the data. Communication: The research assistant will effectively communicate with Dr. Magno regarding data collection in a professional and clear manor. Required Qualifications Applicants must be accepted into a graduate program at Gannon University. Ideal candidates will be highly motivated, possess strong organizational skills, and demonstrate the ability to work independently. Additionally, candidates must align with and support the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Ability to lift 20 pounds if needed Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Support Service Position Type GA (Research, Teaching, Athletic Training) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours- Depends on Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
