    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14914": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Program Assistant",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Program Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Program Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Program Assistant Posting Number AS1133P Subdivision School of Engineering and Computing Division Col. of Engineering & Business Department Environmental Science & Engr. Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Gannon University, a Catholic university, invites applications for a full-time Program Assistant in the School of Engineering and Computing housed in the College of Engineering and Business. The successful candidate will work closely with the academic leadership, faculty and students to provide support to all aspects of the programs. The position is responsible for supporting the operations of academic departments (Computer and Information Science, Electrical and Cyber Engineering, and Environmental Science and Engineering, Mechanical Engineering and Biomedical, Industrial and System Engineering), including the application of policies and procedures, and some general administrative tasks. A sophisticated knowledge of Excel and ability to manage and understand data is essential. Must possess a willingness to learn other technology. Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Requirements include effective communication skills, strong interpersonal and organizational skills and the ability to maintain confidentiality; the ability to work independently; the capability to prioritize and manage multiple tasks simultaneously; familiarity with social media management, and excellent decision-making and problem-solving ability. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : Communications & Editing: Manage internal and external communications across email, digital signage, and social media. Draft and proofread correspondence, reports, and promotional materials. Design flyers and graphics. Update BrightSigns with relevant content. Data Management & Reporting: Generate and analyze reports. Retrieve data from internal systems and external databases to support leadership decisions. Summarize findings for accreditation, assessment, and performance metrics. Meetings & Coordination: Schedule and coordinate in-person and virtual meetings. Prepare agendas and presentation materials, send invitations, and manage logistics. Attend meetings to take minutes and distribute follow-up documentation. Academic Documentation: Edit academic documents including catalog entries, programs and curriculum sheets, and schedules. Assist leadership with accreditation reports, unit reviews, and program documentation. Process project and thesis records when applicable. Supervisor & Leadership Support: Support academic leadership by preparing materials for review and approval. Facilitate follow-through on approved items including communications and document distribution. Records Management: Maintain departmental records including adjunct resumes, syllabi, and student files where applicable. Ensure proper storage and retrieval of faculty and program data. Office Administration & Purchasing: Oversee supplies and inventory for faculty and staff. Manage budgets, process invoices and reimbursements, and prepare check requisitions. Make informed purchasing decisions as needed. Facilities & Technology Liaison: Coordinate maintenance and technology needs with Physical Plant and ITS . Serve as point of contact for vendors and IT service requests relevant to department operations. Event Planning & Support: Plan, execute, and support departmental and college events. Coordinate with other Gannon/community/industry partners for special events. Arrange logistics, handle registrations, book facilities, coordinate food service, and assist with event setup/takedown. Communicate event details to stakeholders. Marketing & Outreach: Create promotional campaigns and materials for recruitment and public outreach. Manage departmental social media, prepare mailings, and collaborate with faculty to showcase student and faculty achievements. Monitor and manage the School of Business website pages. Student Retention Support: Support retention efforts through planning, promoting and executing student-focused events. Gather student feedback through surveys or focus groups. Staffing & Onboarding Support: Assist with staffing processes by posting job openings for graduate assistants and student workers. For new employees, schedule interviews, manage onboarding paperwork, and coordinate communications with the dean’s office and HR. Special Projects & Strategic Initiatives: Participate in committees as assigned. Lead or support initiatives to automate or streamline processes. Create documentation to educate faculty, staff, and students on new systems and processes. General Duties: Performs other tasks as assigned within the scope of the position as needed. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : Under general supervision, this position reports to the academic leadership but may receive specific instructions from other professionals within the department. This position may assign and check the work of student workers. CONTACT WITH OTHERS : Internal: Works with faculty, staff, administration and students. Will respond to requests for service or securing services or information from other departments across the University. External: Works with the general public, responding to inquiries (prospective students, parents, etc.) Works with alumni, industry and community partners ( SEC academic programs’ Advisory Board Members) and guests on campus, interfaces with Gannon affiliate entities ( SBDC , Beehive) and companies. Required Qualifications Education: Associate’s degree. Experience: Three years of general secretarial experience; proficiency in using personal computers and application software, such as Microsoft Excel, Word, PowerPoint and Outlook is required. Skills: Must possess excellent verbal, written, proofreading, and organizational skills; the ability to craft correspondence and reports independently with minimal supervision; the ability to read and comprehend work orders, written instructions and procedure manuals; the ability to record accurate meeting minutes and disseminate information to stakeholders; the ability to multitask and prioritize responsibilities, ability to ask direction if a course of action is unclear; the ability to research and compile data; and communicate with diverse populations. This position is extremely self-directed. The assumption is that the incumbent will thrive in an environment where they are largely autonomous and proactive. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications A bachelor’s degree is preferred with prior experience in higher education settings. Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS : Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy office and University environment. WORKING CONDITIONS : Work is performed in a busy office setting. Occasional weekend and evening hours are required. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Support Office Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule 8:00AM-4:30PM, Monday through Friday Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please rate your experience with Microsoft Office Suite products. Excellent, over 7 years extensive experience with most products Very Good, 5 to 7 years experience and comfortable with most products Good, 3 to 5 years solid experience with Outlook, Word, and Excel Fair, more then 3 years experience with Outlook, Word, and Excel Poor, I have not had a lot of exposure to Microsoft Office Suite Describe your proficiency with Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Teams. Please provide specific examples of how you have used these applications to improve efficiency, manage data, create reports or presentations, coordinate projects, or support leadership in a professional or academic environment. (Open Ended Question) Higher education relies on strategic communications to recruit students and engage alumni, employers, and community partners. Describe how you would use social media, digital communications, and other marketing tools to increase visibility and engagement for an academic department. Include examples of successful campaigns you have managed or ideas you would implement in this role. (Open Ended Question) Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15178": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Academic &amp; Career Development Peer Mentor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Academic & Career Development Peer Mentor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is best suited for someone able to multitask, interested in fashion and retail, and who enjoys working with students in a one-on-one setting. Position Details Position Summary Position Title Academic & Career Development Peer Mentor Posting Number Division Career & Employment Services Department Provost & Student Experience (AA) Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Position Summary: We are seeking enthusiastic and dependable student leaders to join our Academic and Career Development ( ACD ) team as Academic and Career Development Peer Mentors. This role includes taking the lead in conducting Career Closet appointments and ensuring that professional wardrobe support is accessible and welcoming to all students. This position will also gain hands-on experience by personally guiding and supporting students through resume review and career resource education. This position offers valuable experience in communication, career coaching, customer service, public speaking, and office administration while helping promote a supportive and inclusive campus environment. Key Responsibilities: Career Closet Management · Assist students in selecting appropriate professional attire from the Career Closet. · Maintain an inclusive, equitable, and organized space that reflects the university’s values. · Collaborate with professional staff to manage inventory and donations: folding, steaming, tagging, restocking, and tracking incoming and outgoing items. · Write and mail donation thank you notes. Career Peer Support · Serve as a consultant for students seeking help with resumes, cover letters, professional fashion, and student employment preparation. · Conduct one-on-one professional development sessions with students and input notes in Handshake. · Educate students on key career resources (e.g., Handshake, PeopleAdmin, etc). Office Operations & Customer Service · Support professional staff in brainstorming and creating content ideas for social media and career fair promotions. · Demonstrate a high level of professionalism and maintain strict confidentiality in all student interactions and data handling. Career Readiness Competency Goals: In alignment with the National Association of Colleges and Employers ( NACE ) competencies, student employees in this position will develop: · Communication : Through peer coaching, presentations, and professional correspondence. · · Technology : Via hands-on use of Handshake, Excel, and other digital career tools. · Professionalism : Demonstrated through professional dress, confidentiality, and time management. · Equity & Inclusion : By supporting a welcoming and inclusive environment in both career coaching and the Career Closet. · Critical Thinking : When tailoring a resume and clothing guidance to individual student needs. Required Qualifications Qualifications: · Advanced written and verbal communication skills · Strong organizational and customer service skills · Demonstrated campus leadership or involvement · Familiarity with Microsoft Office, specifically Excel; willingness to learn new platforms · Commitment to confidentiality and respect for sensitive student information · Creative, proactive mindset with a desire to contribute to team success · Flexible schedule and willingness to grow with the department across semesters · Embodiment of Gannon’s mission and values in daily work Preferred Qualifications - Good academic and conduct records at Gannon - Demonstrated campus leadership experience - Ability to work within a team setting and contribute effectively - Ability to learn and utilize technology platforms that assist in carrying out responsibilities - Must have a flexible schedule and looking to grow with our office in future semesters - Must demonstrate critical thinking skills and be willing to work within a diverse team of individuals - Demonstrate the desire to grow personally and professionally and possess values of living out the Gannon experience -Past experience writing a resume/cover letter for a class assignment or application Physical Demands - Must be able to navigate the office and the entire campus environment with ease as the job requires one to deliver documents, small packages, and run errands from time-to-time. - Must be able to lift up to 50 lbs. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 2 Job Posting Open Date 08/24/2026 Job Posting Close Date 09/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is best suited for someone able to multitask, interested in fashion and retail, and who enjoys working with students in a one-on-one setting. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14416": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Visiting Professor, Psychology",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Visiting Professor, Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Visiting Professor, Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Visiting Professor, Psychology Posting Number F242P Division Dept. of Psychology & Counseling Department Col.Humanities,Ed.&SocScience Location Pepper Pike, OH Position Summary The Gannon University College of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences invites applications for two Visiting Faculty in the Department of Psychology, specialization open, to begin in August 2026 on the Ursuline College campus of Gannon University in Pepper Pike, Ohio. If the anticipated merger between Ursuline College and Gannon University has not taken place by the start date for these positions, the faculty will instead be hired by Ursuline College. The successful candidates will teach Introductory Psychology and other courses in their area of expertise, advise students and prepare them intellectually, professionally, and personally, and will be expected to engage in scholarly activities in keeping with the Boyer Model of Scholarship as is appropriate to the application and receipt of promotion at Gannon. Requirements include a master’s degree or Ph.D. (preferred) in Psychology or related discipline with demonstrated teaching excellence in higher education. ABD candidates may also be considered. Candidates must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its liberal arts and professional education traditions. Gannon University is a Catholic, Diocesan university dedicated to excellence in teaching, scholarship and service. Our faculty and staff prepare students to be global citizens through programs grounded in the liberal arts and sciences and professional specializations. Inspired by the Catholic Intellectual Tradition, we offer a comprehensive, values-centered learning experience that emphasizes faith, leadership, inclusiveness and social responsibility. Gannon University seeks excellence through inclusiveness and invites members of underrepresented groups to apply. Gannon University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For more information about Gannon visit www.gannon.edu . Application Procedure: Submit a cover letter, CV, evidence of excellence in teaching, and the contact information for three professional references to https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/ . Review of applications will begin immediately and this position will remain open until filled. The finalist will be required to submit an original transcript from the institution awarding their terminal degree. References will not be contacted without permission from applicants. Required Qualifications Education: A master’s degree or Ph.D. (preferred) in Psychology or related discipline. Rank: In accordance with the University’s standards, Vice President for Academic Affairs awards initial rank at the time of employment. Licenses and Certifications: As may be required for the discipline. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its strong liberal arts foundation that supports exemplary professional education programs. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy academic environment and necessary travel. Work is performed in a busy classroom and office setting. Tenure Status Temporary Position Type Regular Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 9M Credits Per Year 24 credits Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
