    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15205": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant (Research)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant (Research) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant (Research) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant (Research) Posting Number AS1110P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Physical Therapy Program Location Erie, Pa Position Summary This position is designed to support a scholarship of teaching and learning project. This project examines the implementation of a structured faculty development initiative within the DPT program, referred to as the Education Symposium, designed to strengthen pedagogical knowledge among faculty with varying levels of teaching experience while supporting systematic curriculum review in preparation for CAPTE accreditation. As part of this process, faculty members participate in educational programming around foundational aspects of teaching and learning and complete a structured course analysis that maps course learning objectives. NACE competencies addressed through this position include Critical Thinking, Communication, Teamwork, Technology, Professionalism, and Career & Self-Development. Required Qualifications The applicant demonstrates strong organizational skills, the ability to conduct literature searches and summarize scholarly sources, and proficiency with (or willingness to learn) spreadsheet or database tools. Strong written communication skills and attention to detail are important. The ideal candidate is proactive and self-directed, but comfortable asking for clarification when needed. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Physical demands are minimal and consistent with typical academic and office-based activities. Responsibilities may include prolonged periods of sitting, computer use, reading and reviewing documents, attending meetings, and organizing project materials. No unusual physical demands are anticipated. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Research, Teaching, Athletic Training) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours-Depending on Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
