    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14978": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Clinical Contract Assistant",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Clinical Contract Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Contract Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Clinical Contract Assistant Posting Number AS1144P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Athletic Training Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The successful candidate for this position will work with a dynamic team of staff, faculty and administrators to provide secretarial support for the university. The candidate must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Gannon seeks excellence through inclusiveness and invites members of underrepresented groups to apply. This position is assigned the following essential functions : 1. Creates and maintains clinical contract database of over 700 clinical affiliation agreements for MCHPS Clinical Coordinators. 2. Creates repository of clinical education policies and handbooks for MCHPS Clinical Coordinators. 3. Facilitates communication with MCHPS Clinical Coordinators, Risk Management office, and external organizations to secure signatures on affiliation agreements. 4. Provides the Master of Athletic Training and the Associate of Science in Respiratory Care programs with administrative assistance. 5. Types letters, reports, records, or other related documents from rough draft; modifies form letters to fit varying situations; composes routine correspondence; provides recordings, and/or dictated materials; corrects sentence structure, punctuation, and spelling; proofreads completed materials. 6. Screens and distributes incoming correspondence; fills requests for materials and prepares materials for mailing. 7. Compiles information and prepares various statistical, business, and research reports; types and prepares final reports for supervisor’s approval. 8. Maintains departmental, personnel, and student records and filing systems; maintains financial records for operating and equipment expenses; orders and maintains office supplies and equipment for various laboratories, as needed. 9. Schedules appointments; arranges and participates in conferences and meetings as requested; secures travel arrangements, as needed. 10. Coordinates special events; assists in registration of participants, arranges for physical facilities, housing, and food services to be available, as requested. 11. Greets visitors; maintains cleanliness and organization for the office, answers telephone; refers callers to proper persons based on type of information requests; answers inquiries requiring standard factual information; takes messages. 12. Aids in the recruitment and hiring of student workers, as needed. 13. Facilitates and maintains accreditation files, updates accreditation software when needed, and works to support accreditation and/or specialty certification needs as required. 14. Provides full secretarial support using Microsoft Office software applications, including but not limited to, Excel, Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, Forms, Teams, as well as university services software such as Colleague, PeopleAdmin and other program-specific software and/or online platforms. 15. Performs other duties as assigned within the scope and responsibility and requirements of the job. Required Qualifications Qualifications | Education : Educational background equivalent to a high school degree/ GED with specialized courses in bookkeeping, word-processing, and office procedures. Experience : Three years of general secretarial experience with a working knowledge of Microsoft Office products (e.g., Word, EXCEL , PowerPoint, Teams, Forms) and office equipment (e.g., telephone, computer, calculator and copier, etc.). Skills : Must possess excellent verbal, written, proofreading and organizational skills; the ability to read and comprehend work orders, written instructions and procedure manuals; the ability to transcribe correspondence and enter data into records and logs with accuracy; the ability to perform basic mathematical calculations; the ability to multitask and prioritize responsibilities; ability to seek direction regarding courses of action; and the ability to research and compile data. University Mission : Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s degree in business or related area. Experience with contract management including maintenance of contract management software or databases. Physical Demands Candidates must be able to meet the physical and technical demands of busy office and university environment. Reasonable accommodations, in accordance with ADA requirements, may be made upon request to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Support Office Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule 8-4:30, Monday thru Friday Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Optional Documents Transcripts Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15184": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | McNair Scholars Graduate Student Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help McNair Scholars Graduate Student Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. N/A Position Details Position Summary Position Title McNair Scholars Graduate Student Posting Number Division Dean's Office; MCHPS Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Critical Thinking – Identify and respond to program and student needs by considering situational context, evaluating relevant information, and applying sound judgment. The graduate assistant will strengthen these skills through student engagement, program planning, recruitment, interviewing prospective scholars, and day-to-day program operations. Equity & Inclusion – Demonstrate the ability to engage and support students effectively while promoting access, belonging, and academic success. Critical thinking and effective student engagement are central to this role. Through mentoring, programming, recruitment, and communication, the graduate assistant will support scholars’ academic and professional development. Program Purpose The Ronald E. McNair Postbaccalaureate Achievement Program prepares eligible undergraduate students for graduate education, with an emphasis on doctoral study. The program provides research experiences, graduate school preparation, academic and professional development, mentoring, and other services designed to help scholars successfully pursue advanced degrees. Responsibilities The graduate assistant will support the overall operation of the McNair Scholars Program, including: Scholar Support & Mentoring: Mentor scholars and assist with graduate school preparation, academic and professional development, and connection to appropriate university resources. Recruitment: Support recruitment and outreach efforts, including communicating with prospective scholars and participating in interviews. Programming: Assist with planning, coordinating, and facilitating workshops, events, research-related activities, and other program initiatives. Social Media & Communications: Manage program social media and develop digital content highlighting scholar accomplishments, research experiences, graduate school preparation, program activities, and recruitment opportunities. Records & Program Tracking: Maintain accurate student records and assist with tracking scholar participation, services, and program activities. Campus & Community Engagement: Communicate with faculty, university departments, and external organizations to support scholar and program needs. Program Operations: Provide administrative and operational support for program initiatives and other responsibilities as assigned. Required Qualifications Demonstrate the ability to engage and collaborate effectively with others. Candidate must be enrolled at Gannon University in a graduate program full-time. Additionally, candidate must have a cumulative GPA of at least 3.00. The qualified candidate will demonstrate evidence of excellent written and oral communication skills; strong interpersonal, organizational, and analytical skills; demonstrated ability to be self-motivated. Some travel is required. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands N/A Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Job Posting Open Date 09/03/2026 Job Posting Close Date 10/05/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants N/A Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14561": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Head Coach, Competitive Dance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Head Coach, Competitive Dance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Head Coach, Competitive Dance Posting Number AS1102P Subdivision Athletic Director's Office Division Athletics Department Competitive Cheer and Stunt Location Erie, Pa Position Summary This is a full-time 12 month position and is responsible for coaching, managing and directing all aspects of the Gannon University Competitive Dance team. The program competes at the intercollegiate II level and attends the NCA & NDA Collegiate Championship. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : 1. Recruits quality academic students who are also competitive student-athletes. 2. Schedules all competitive events and competitive facilities. 3. Schedules all practices and practice facilities. 4. Coordinates advanced scheduling, with budget approval, for all transportation, hotel, and meal requirements for away contests. 5. Completes all expense reports for all expenses associated with home and away contests. 6. Purchases, issues, maintains, and collects all team uniforms and equipment. 7. Oversees program budget and all related activities. 8. Teaches advanced level technical skills in a variety of categories: pom, jazz, and hip hop. 9. Choreographs any performances and provides choreography support for competitive routines. 10. Monitors and supports all student-athletes in their academic pursuits. 11. Monitors, educates, and advises all student-athletes concerning expectations in the classroom, during competitions and practices, and within campus and community living. 12. Advises administration of any significant accomplishments (athletic, academic, civic) obtained by any member of the team. 13. Identifies, hires, and supervises full-time staff, volunteer(s), manager(s), and/or student assistant(s). 14. Participates in an annual review of the season with the Athletic Administration. 15. Learns, understands, and complies with all rules and regulations set forth by NDA and Gannon University. 16. Passes the NCAA educational modules on an annual basis. 17. Develop and implement camps and clinics. 18. Works collaboratively to develop and implement initiatives that support the program – alumni engagement, development, and promotional. 19. Performs other duties related as assigned. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS : Education: A Bachelor’s degree is required; a Master’s degree is preferred. Experience: Successful collegiate-level coaching experience is required. Skills: Must have excellent communication skills and technical knowledge of sport-specific skills identified above for dance, combined with the ability to effectively teach and coach them. Licenses and Certifications : A valid driver’s license in good standing. Per Gannon’s Institutional Policy Manual there can be no suspensions on the Motor Vehicle Record for 5 years prior to being hired. Must successfully complete the USA Gymnastics’ safety course. AED / CPR /First Aid Certified. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Three to five years of collegiate coaching experience. Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS : Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy athletic team schedule. WORKING CONDITIONS : Work is performed indoors and outdoors in a busy University setting. The work schedule will vary with heavier emphasis September through April. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week varies Work Schedule varies Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15092": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | STEM Center - Tutor - Major: Physician Asst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help STEM Center - Tutor - Major: Physician Asst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Position Details Position Summary Position Title STEM Center - Tutor - Major: Physician Asst Posting Number Division Library Department Provost & Student Experience (AA) Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Believe in your own knowledge and perseverance, and the amazing potential of Gannon students Lead Gannon students to conquer their academic hurdles, both small and large Unleash your love for your major and your favorite courses Enjoy making a deep impact on a very flexible schedule Key responsibilities and highlights: Tutor peers in STEM subject material they are qualified to cover May seek or perform other necessary STEM Center work, with approval Some initial and ongoing (paid) training is likely to be required Position structure: Will have one regular paid guaranteed shift per week (likely 3 hours, and in the late afternoon and early evening such as 4-7PM on a Sunday-Thursday); work during this shift will be tutoring, preparation/training, other tasks to support the STEM Center and our stakeholders, or other work to benefit the University Needs to establish additional availability within library hours of operation for “on-call” tutoring (paid for actual tutoring appointments only; up to ~3 additional hours if holding appointments, more may be possible but cannot be guaranteed) There will basically be one such tutor per major (one per set of similar majors) for each area traditionally served by the STEM Center Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Critical Thinking/Problem Solving: A STEM tutor can develop critical thinking and problem-solving skills by breaking down complex concepts for students, identifying gaps in their understanding, and helping them develop strategies to solve problems. Oral/Written Communication: STEM tutors need to clearly explain complex ideas and concepts to students within tutoring sessions and in interactions with coworkers and STEM Center management. Tutors may be required to speak to classes, reach out to students, and represent the STEM Center at functions or events. Additionally, tutors may be required to send emails, make phone calls, or initiate other communication on behalf of the STEM Center. Teamwork/Collaboration: STEM tutors can facilitate or assist with group study sessions and participate in other projects or initiatives to support the STEM Center. Digital Technology: Tutors may create online resources, utilizing software or apps to visualize concepts, and must make extensive use of scheduling systems, MS Teams, and other software to perform essential functions of the job. Leadership: In working with a variety of students, tutors have regular opportunity to thrive in changing environments, to identify and address complex problems, and to navigate ambiguity. Professionalism/Work Ethic: By being punctual, prepared, and professional in their interactions with students, tutors can showcase a strong work ethic. They must also adhere to ethical guidelines and respect the confidentiality of their students. Career Management: The STEM Center is a cocurricular opportunity to develop and showcase the ability to build success in others and specifically to teach or train others. Tutoring course material often builds additional competencies in those areas. Global/Intercultural Fluency: To develop global and intercultural fluency, tutors often have opportunities to work with a diverse slate of Gannon students, learning, understanding, and adapting to academic and nonacademic facets of culture and communication. Required Qualifications Major and significant course load matching position title High GPA and positive reputation with faculty Interpersonal excellence Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands N/A Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Job Posting Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Have you or will you soon complete the REQUIRED questionnaire at: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV ? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15207": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant, PA Program - Ruskin (Administrative)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant, PA Program - Ruskin (Administrative) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant, PA Program - Ruskin (Administrative) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We are accepting applications only from students at Gannon's Ruskin location who are not in the Physician Assistant program. Please submit two letters of recommendation along with your resumé. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant, PA Program - Ruskin (Administrative) Posting Number AS1109P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Physician Assistant Prgm-Ruskn Location Ruskin, Fl Position Summary This individual provides administrative support to the PA program faculty, Clinical Coordinators, Program Director, and Administrative Assistant. The GA may also assist with any and all projects associated with Gannon University’s Ruskin, FL, location. This individual CANNOT be enrolled in the Physician Assistant program. Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Critical Thinking, Communication, Teamwork, and Technology - The GA will build and maintain collaborative relationships with PA faculty and staff and other student workers, and will use systems to monitor and document inventory of supplies. The GA will clearly and effectively exchange information with the staff they are assisting in preparation of orders. Professionalism - The GA will demonstrate integrity, accountability, and effective work habits by documenting hours and tasks worked, and communicating with the GA supervisor(s) at least weekly. • This position runs through the academic year, up to five hours a week, during campus office hours. Exceptions are at the discretion of the GA supervisors. • Responsibilities include filing, copying, making labels, creating/editing files and spreadsheets, monitor and document inventory of supplies, preparing orders for and restocking of lab supplies, and maintaining an effective working environment. • Demonstrate a proactive and positive attitude. • Included in the work hours are regular meetings scheduled with one or more of the Graduate Assistantship supervisor(s): the PA Program Director (“PD”) and Secretary. • All GAs must sign a FERPA (Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act) agreement to protect student confidentiality at all times. Required Qualifications This position requires someone who is highly organized and able to manage several tasks/projects at one time. He or she will work with the PA faculty, the Clinical Coordinators, and the PA Secretary managing files, creating and updating documents, and tracking student documents related to clinical rotations. The person in this position has to be comfortable representing Gannon University in a professional way with community organizations. Strong skills of attention to detail and personal initiative are a must for this position. Preferred Qualifications Proficiency in Microsoft Office (i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.) and previous administrative experience are preferred. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Administrative) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 10M Hours per Week 5 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Letter of Recommendation Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How many years of experience do you have working in an office environment? 1-2 3-5 6-8 More than 10 Please briefly describe your experience using Excel. (Open Ended Question) It can be challenging to balance work and studies.  How have you done this in the past, and how do you plan to handle it if you are hired? (Open Ended Question) Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14855": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Athletics Media Relations Student Assistant",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Athletics Media Relations Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Athletics Media Relations Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If selected for an interview, the candidate will be contacted by the Athletic Media Relations Office. If you are hired, your continued employment may be contingent on you remaining eligible for Federal Work Study. Position Details Position Summary Position Title Athletics Media Relations Student Assistant Posting Number Division Athletic Director's Office Department Athletics Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Communication: Clearly and effectively exchange information, queries and/or perspectives with supervisors and co-workers before, during, and after sporting events. Let supervisors know which tasks are more challenging and help them develop a plan to meet expectations. Career and Self-Development: After being instructed on the technical aspects of the job, the student employee should take the initiative to learn a wider depth of knowledge about the technology being utilized or learn about other desired technical positions. Gannon students only. Assists the Director of Athletics for Media Relations (Sports Information Office) with game operations/management for the University’s NCAA Division II athletics program. The position will be responsible for game management that includes but is not limited to the PSAC Network webcasts technical direction, webcast camera work, video recording for highlights, scoreboard operation, play clock operation, statistical input, game music director, video board operation, and media assistance. Additionally, the position will work to ensure compliance with NCAA , PSAC , and Title IX requirements relative to athletic communications. Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Availability to work nights and weekends is a must. Required Qualifications * If you are hired, your continued employment may be contingent on you remaining eligible for Federal Work Study. 1. Reliability 2. Timeliness 3. Ability to multitask 4. Sports knowledge 5. Ability to learn technical skills quickly 6. Ability to work as a team member and independently Preferred Qualifications 1. Scoreboard operation 2. Play clock operation 3. Photography and/or videography for events 4. Music direction during events 5. Statistical input for sporting events 6. Camera work during live webcasts 7. Play-by-play announcing for live streams for a variety of sports 8. Technical direction for webcasts 9. Videoboard/graphics board operation 10. Ability to write/edit copy. Physical Demands 1. Must be able to work in a variety of weather conditions (rain, snow, cold, sun, etc.). 2. Must be able to climb stairs and bleachers steps. 3. Must have no fear of heights. 4. Must be able to stand for two to three hours. 5. Must be willing to learn about new sports. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 10 Job Posting Open Date 08/04/2026 Job Posting Close Date 10/15/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants If selected for an interview, the candidate will be contacted by the Athletic Media Relations Office. If you are hired, your continued employment may be contingent on you remaining eligible for Federal Work Study. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you available to work nights? Yes No * Are you willing and interested in learning how to stat NCAA competitions? Yes No * Are you comfortable working with a videoboard? Yes No * Do you you qualify or are you eligible for Federal Work Study? Yes No Unsure Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
