l, prepared, and professional in their interactions with students, tutors can showcase a strong work ethic. They must also adhere to ethical guidelines and respect the confidentiality of their students. Career Management: The STEM Center is a cocurricular opportunity to develop and showcase the ability to build success in others and specifically to teach or train others. Tutoring course material often builds additional competencies in those areas. Global/Intercultural Fluency: To develop global and intercultural fluency, tutors often have opportunities to work with a diverse slate of Gannon students, learning, understanding, and adapting to academic and nonacademic facets of culture and communication. Required Qualifications Flexibility, punctuality, and ethics Preferred Qualifications Previous Calculus Readiness proctoring experience Physical Demands N/A Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 4 Job Posting Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Posting Close Date 01/29/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants N/A Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
