    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14591": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Faculty Teaching Track - Villa Maria School of Nursing and Coordinator Patient Simulation Center",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Faculty Teaching Track - Villa Maria School of Nursing and Coordinator Patient Simulation Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Teaching Track - Villa Maria School of Nursing and Coordinator Patient Simulation Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Faculty Teaching Track - Villa Maria School of Nursing and Coordinator Patient Simulation Center Posting Number F245P Division School of Health Professions Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Gannon University is committed to excellence in student-centered learning with an emphasis on student-learning outcomes. The faculty work collaboratively with colleagues; deliver instruction; advise students; and engage in professional, University, and community service activities. All faculty must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its liberal arts and professional education traditions. The Villa Maria School of Nursing currently has one 12-month faculty position available which will be responsible for teaching in both the undergraduate and the graduate programs and clinical education, as assigned. Candidates must provide evidence of competence in diverse teaching methods and effective classroom and clinical instruction. Additionally, this position will serve as the coordinator for the Patient Simulation Center. The Patient Simulation Center includes 14 medium- and high-fidelity patient simulators, intravenous training stations, simulated emergency rooms, and simulated labor/delivery/recovery rooms. The coordinator will support scheduling, education, and simulation facilitation activities for academic programs across the Morosky College of Health Professions and Sciences. Required Qualifications Must be a registered nurse with a master’s degree in nursing. Must possess or be eligible to obtain nursing licensure in Pennsylvania. Must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its liberal arts and professional education traditions. Preferred Qualifications An earned doctorate in nursing or a closely related field; applicants who are enrolled or in the process of enrolling to doctoral programs are also encouraged to apply. Recent clinical and teaching experience in a program of higher education. Experience with simulation instruction and conducting simulation in an educational environment Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy academic and clinical environment. Tenure Status Teaching Track Position Type Regular Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Credits Per Year 27 Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Optional Documents Resume Transcripts Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
