    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14757": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Secretary, Doctor of Physical Therapy Program, Erie, PA Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Secretary, Doctor of Physical Therapy Program, Erie, PA Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Secretary, Doctor of Physical Therapy Program, Erie, PA Posting Number AS1116P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Dr. of Physical Therapy Location Erie, Pa Position Summary POSITION SUMMARY : The secretary provides secretarial and administrative support for an academic or administrative unit(s). Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : 1. Accurately and independently prepares communications and reports for assigned academic unit(s), including accreditation and clinical education. 2. Prepares and maintains accurate student, faculty, and program files/data consistent with accreditation and university expectations. 3. Prioritizes task initiation and completion consistent with needs of the university and academic unit(s). 4. Provides assigned academic unit(s) assistance with management of purchases, expenses, inventory, and budget data; monitors and maintains budget and inventory documentation. 5. Provides assigned academic unit(s) and student body with inquiries, data (as appropriate), exam proctoring, and onboarding requirements for clinical partners. 6. Facilitates necessary and accurate communication to and among university offices to support seamless operations and services to our students, employees, guests, and community partners. 7. Assists academic unit(s) with event planning and coordination; available as necessary for university event assistance. 8. Performs other duties as assigned within the scope and responsibility, and requirements of the job. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : This position works under limited supervision but may receive instruction from and support other professionals. This position may assign and check work of student workers and graduate assistants. CONTACT WITH OTHERS : Internal: Has contact with administrators of all levels, faculty, staff, and students, exchanging information and resolving problems, and responding to requests for service. External: Has contact with general public, responding to inquiries or arranging meetings, and securing information. Required Qualifications Education: Educational background equivalent to a high school degree/ GED with specialized courses in bookkeeping, typing/word-processing, and office procedures. Business school training is preferred. Experience: Three years of general secretarial experience; a working knowledge of Microsoft Office products and office equipment (e.g., computer, calculator, copier equipment, etc.). Skills: Must possess excellent verbal, written, proofreading and organizational skills; the ability to read and comprehend work orders, written instructions, and procedure manuals; the ability to transcribe correspondence and enter data into records and logs with accuracy; the ability to perform basic mathematical calculations; the ability to multitask and prioritize responsibilities, seeking direction regarding courses of action; the ability to research and compile data; and the ability to interpret and communicate policy as directed. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Experience in a college or university environment preferred. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a normal office environment. Work is performed in a busy office setting. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Support Office Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule 8-4:30, Monday thru Friday Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
