      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Research Assistant for Evaluation of Energy-Efficient AI Accelerators for Machine Learning Systems (Dr. Mariam Manakkadu)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Research Assistant for Evaluation of Energy-Efficient AI Accelerators for Machine Learning Systems (Dr. Mariam Manakkadu) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Research Assistant for Evaluation of Energy-Efficient AI Accelerators for Machine Learning Systems (Dr. Mariam Manakkadu) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Category 1 for mariamma001@gannon.edu Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Research Assistant for Evaluation of Energy-Efficient AI Accelerators for Machine Learning Systems (Dr. Mariam Manakkadu) Posting Number AS1111P Subdivision School of Engineering and Computing Division Col. of Engineering & Business Department Computer & Information Science Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Computer and Information Science Student assistant job description should include, but not be limited to: Strong programming skills in Python and C/C++ Familiarity with machine learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow Ability to read, analyze, and summarize research literature Strong analytical, problem-solving, and documentation skills • Researching, designing, implementing, and managing software programs • Read research papers • Analyze and generate solution to the given problem • Browse GitHub repositories and collect data, apply data mining and machine learning techniques as required • Writing and implementing efficient scripts • Determining operational practicality • Developing quality assurance procedures • Deploying software tools, processes, and metrics • Maintaining and upgrading existing systems • Working closely with other developers and professor • Excellent writing skill in English NACE Competencies: 1. Critical Thinking: Multi-task well in a fast-paced autonomous environment. 2. Professionalism: Prioritize and complete tasks to accomplish organizational goals. Dissemination of Results Present the outcomes of your experience at Celebrate Gannon and/or other venues determined by the college. Required Qualifications Grad student Proficiency C++, Java, Python Preferred Qualifications N/A Physical Demands none Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Research, Teaching, Athletic Training) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
