      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | STEM Center - Tutor - Major: CIS, Software Eng Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help STEM Center - Tutor - Major: CIS, Software Eng Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Position Details Position Summary Position Title STEM Center - Tutor - Major: CIS, Software Eng Posting Number Division Library Department Provost & Student Experience (AA) Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Believe in your own knowledge and perseverance, and the amazing potential of Gannon students Lead Gannon students to conquer their academic hurdles, both small and large Unleash your love for your major and your favorite courses Enjoy making a deep impact on a very flexible schedule Key responsibilities and highlights: Tutor peers in STEM subject material they are qualified to cover May seek or perform other necessary STEM Center work, with approval Some initial and ongoing (paid) training is likely to be required Position structure: Will have one regular paid guaranteed shift per week (likely 3 hours, and in the late afternoon and early evening such as 4-7PM on a Sunday-Thursday); work during this shift will be tutoring, preparation/training, other tasks to support the STEM Center and our stakeholders, or other work to benefit the University Needs to establish additional availability within library hours of operation for “on-call” tutoring (paid for actual tutoring appointments only; up to ~3 additional hours if holding appointments, more may be possible but cannot be guaranteed) There will basically be one such tutor per major (one per set of similar majors) for each area traditionally served by the STEM Center Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Critical Thinking/Problem Solving: A STEM tutor can develop critical thinking and problem-solving skills by breaking down complex concepts for students, identifying gaps in their understanding, and helping them develop strategies to solve problems. Oral/Written Communication: STEM tutors need to clearly explain complex ideas and concepts to students within tutoring sessions and in interactions with coworkers and STEM Center management. Tutors may be required to speak to classes, reach out to students, and represent the STEM Center at functions or events. Additionally, tutors may be required to send emails, make phone calls, or initiate other communication on behalf of the STEM Center. Teamwork/Collaboration: STEM tutors can facilitate or assist with group study sessions and participate in other projects or initiatives to support the STEM Center. Digital Technology: Tutors may create online resources, utilizing software or apps to visualize concepts, and must make extensive use of scheduling systems, MS Teams, and other software to perform essential functions of the job. Leadership: In working with a variety of students, tutors have regular opportunity to thrive in changing environments, to identify and address complex problems, and to navigate ambiguity. Professionalism/Work Ethic: By being punctual, prepared, and professional in their interactions with students, tutors can showcase a strong work ethic. They must also adhere to ethical guidelines and respect the confidentiality of their students. Career Management: The STEM Center is a cocurricular opportunity to develop and showcase the ability to build success in others and specifically to teach or train others. Tutoring course material often builds additional competencies in those areas. Global/Intercultural Fluency: To develop global and intercultural fluency, tutors often have opportunities to work with a diverse slate of Gannon students, learning, understanding, and adapting to academic and nonacademic facets of culture and communication. Required Qualifications Major and significant course load matching position title High GPA and positive reputation with faculty Interpersonal excellence Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands N/A Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Job Posting Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Have you or will you soon complete the REQUIRED questionnaire at: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV ? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15216": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Assistant Professor/Clinical Coordinator in Physician Assistant (Ruskin, FL)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assistant Professor/Clinical Coordinator in Physician Assistant (Ruskin, FL) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor/Clinical Coordinator in Physician Assistant (Ruskin, FL) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Professor/Clinical Coordinator in Physician Assistant (Ruskin, FL) Posting Number F256P Division School of Health Professions Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Ruskin, Fl Position Summary Gannon University’s Morosky College of Health Professions and Sciences invites applications for a full-time Clinical Coordinator and faculty member in the Physician Assistant Program in Ruskin, Florida. The appointment for this twelve-month, tenure-track or teaching-track position begins as early as October 2026. Responsibilities include identifying and developing clinical sites, working with clinical year students according to established standards, preparation of student examinations, and providing research guidance to graduate-level students. The successful candidate will be expected to work collaboratively with colleagues, support an interprofessional learning environment, teach and advise students, and participate in service activities to support the University, community, and profession. Qualified candidates will be expected to engage in scholarly activities in keeping with the Boyer Model of Scholarship as appropriate to the application and receipt of tenure and promotion at Gannon. Gannon University seeks excellence through inclusiveness and invites members of underrepresented groups to apply. Required Qualifications Education/Experience: Master of Physician Assistant Science degree (or equivalent) or a medical degree (M.D. or D.O.) is required; two-to-five (2-5) years of full-time clinical experience is required. Rank: In accordance with the University’s standards, the Provost and Vice President for Student Experience awards initial rank at the time of employment. Licenses and Certifications: Current NCCPA certification is preferable; candidates must have or be eligible for PA, MD, or DO licensure in Florida. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its strong liberal arts foundation that supports exemplary professional education programs. Preferred Qualifications Candidates with a post-professional doctorate degree (PhD, DSc, DHSc, EdD, etc.) are preferred. A minimum of two (2) years of teaching, clinical preceptor, and/or research experience are preferred. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy academic environment. Work is performed in a busy classroom and office setting. Travel to clinical sites may be necessary on occasion. Tenure Status Tenure Track Position Type Regular Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Credits Per Year 24  (tenure track) or 27 (teaching track) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Statement Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14863": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | RWC Building Supervisor - Academic year 26-27 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help RWC Building Supervisor - Academic year 26-27 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Must already work at the RWC as a Building Attendant to apply for this position. Position Details Position Summary Position Title RWC Building Supervisor - Academic year 26-27 Posting Number Division Recreation & Wellness Department Student Development & Engagemt Location Erie, Pa Position Summary POSITION SUMMARY : Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Communication: Clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives with persons inside and outside of the organization. Teamwork: Build and maintain collaborative relationships to work effectively toward common goals, while appreciating diverse viewpoints and shared responsibilities. Professionalism: Knowing work environments differ greatly, understand and demonstrate effective work habits, and act in interest of the larger community and workplace. Responsibilities: The primary responsibility of the Building Supervisor is to provide oversight of the Recreation and Wellness Center during all scheduled shifts. Building Supervisors are responsible for overall daily operations, enforcing facility and University policies and procedures, enacting the safety protocols when appropriate, overseeing Building Attendants and Lifeguards, and any additional tasks that may be assigned. This position will require effective communication at multiple levels. Building Supervisors are expected to be educated on other campus programs and events that may take place in the facility and/or around campus. This position requires high quality customer service, adaptability and quick thinking skills, and the ability to delegate in a variety of ways. Average Hours: 10-14 hours/week ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS 1. Oversee all facility daily operations, which includes direct supervision of Building Attendants, Lifeguards, and all activities and scheduled programming within the facility. 2. Knowledgeable of all Gannon University and Recreation and Wellness Center policies. Must enforce and apply all policies and procedures during scheduled shift. 3. Demonstrate leadership skills, written and verbal communication skills, customer service skills, problem solving, and the ability to work a variety of groups which include with students, University faculty and staff, and all external members. 4. Assist with all accidents, injuries, and incidents in emergency situations while on duty. This position is the main correspondent with Gannon Police and Safety and are responsible for submitting reports as needed. 5. Required to attend all mandatory staff meeting and staff trainings. 6. Be able to effectively and accurately communicate information in person or over the phone regarding facility hours, facility programming, and available amenities. 7. Responsible for Front Desk sales which include: completing memberships, guest passes, miscellaneous sales, locker rentals, and special programming. 8. Ensure money intake is accurate at all times and closing Building Supervisors will be responsible for the nightly deposit. 9. Required to train Building Attendants on all job responsibilities and turn in appropriate training list into Graduate Assistant of Personnel. May be required to assist in Building Attendant and Lifeguard performance evaluations. 10. Be able to report when equipment and supplies are running low or when equipment replacements are needed. 11. Complete mandatory student development and engagement credits per semester. 12. Provide a professional, welcoming, and inclusive environment for all who enter the facility. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS : Education: Enrolled as a full-time student of Gannon University preferably with a minimum of a 2.5 GPA . Experience: This position is a promotional opportunity from the Building Attendant position. Experience must include use of Microsoft Word, Excel, and use of standard office equipment such as copy machine, printer, and telephone. Previous customer service, recreation, or fitness experience preferred. Certifications: Certified in CPR & AED *Training offered upon hire Skills: Leadership skills including strong verbal and written communication skills, working in a team atmosphere, and professionalism. Individual must be able to work with a diverse population that would include students, faculty, staff, and community members. Must be able to work independently without direct supervision on day to day tasks and be able to take initiative. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS : Ability to lift and carry weight, possibly up to 50lbs unassisted Ability to walk, stand, and move about for approximately 2-8 hours; without access to a chair Ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl Ability to climb (stairs/ladders) or balance Ability to walk around building and potentially across campus Repetitive movement of hands, arms and legs, such as sweeping, vacuuming, and moping Meet the physical demands associated with a busy office and University environment. WORKING CONDITIONS : Work is performed in a busy campus-wide setting. All facility hours are covered by this position and flexibility is required for hours. Must be a team player and be willing to cover or trade shifts when necessary. Must be available to work days, evenings, weekends, and campus holiday breaks as necessary. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 20 Job Posting Open Date 08/07/2026 Job Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Must already work at the RWC as a Building Attendant to apply for this position. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you eligible for Federal Work Study as determined by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Unsure * What would be your most significant contribution or positive aspect that you would bring to our program? (Open Ended Question) * List all experiences with Recreation and Wellness Center programs and activities you have taken a part of (group fitness classes, intramural sports, sport clubs, special events, etc.) (Open Ended Question) * Is there anything that may interfere with your work availability at the Recreation and Wellness Center (other jobs, internships, observations, meeting, clubs, etc.)? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently certified in American Red Cross CPR/AED?  If so, when do they expire?  If not, do you agree to get certified before starting work?  Will you need training from the RWC? (Open Ended Question) * Are you able and willing to do heavy lifting and moving when the job requires it? yes no * Feel free to list any additional comments that you feel would help us in placing you in a staff position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
