    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15049": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant - 2nd Year Anatomy - FA 26 (Tutoring and Lab Assistants)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant - 2nd Year Anatomy - FA 26 (Tutoring and Lab Assistants) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant - 2nd Year Anatomy - FA 26 (Tutoring and Lab Assistants) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant - 2nd Year Anatomy - FA 26 (Tutoring and Lab Assistants) Posting Number AS1155P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Physical Therapy Program Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Doctor of Physical Therapy Program at Gannon University is committed to excellence in student-centered learning, with an emphasis on student learning outcomes. Graduate Assistants play an important role in achieving these outcomes by working collaboratively with program faculty and fellow Graduate Assistants to support program operations, facilitate open laboratory experiences, provide academic support as requested by faculty, and assist with clinical practice opportunities. While each Graduate Assistant has primary responsibilities, all GAs are expected to work collaboratively, support one another, and contribute to program needs as they arise. As leaders and representatives of the DPT Program, Graduate Assistants are expected to demonstrate professionalism, initiative, flexibility, maintain student confidentiality, and conduct themselves in a manner that reflects the standards and values of the program. This position is for students beginning the second year of the DPT program. Career Readiness Competencies Communication: Effectively communicate with faculty, peers, and students while demonstrating respect for diverse learning styles, communication abilities, and cultural backgrounds. Teamwork: Collaborate with faculty and fellow Graduate Assistants to support program operations, assist one another as needed, and contribute to shared program goals. Professionalism: Demonstrate initiative, flexibility, dependability, confidentiality, and timely completion of responsibilities while serving as a leader and representative of the DPT Program. Responsibilities in the fall semester: 1. Ensure that all students follow laboratory safety guidelines, wear appropriate attire, including long pants, closed-toed shoes, and eye protection, and maintain professional conduct during scheduled laboratory times. 2. Complete cadaver dissections according to provided instructions. The second-year anatomy Graduate Assistant is expected to mentor the first-year Graduate Assistant in completing dissections. 3. Assist with open laboratory sessions for first-year anatomy students and ensure adherence to laboratory safety expectations. 4. Assist with maintaining an inventory of essential laboratory materials, including nitrile gloves and dissection kits. 5. Ensure that all laboratory surfaces and tools are properly cleaned and disinfected following dissections and open laboratory sessions. 6. Assist faculty with administrative tasks, grading, and other responsibilities as assigned. Responsibilities in the spring Semester 1. Assist with maintaining physical therapy laboratory environments, including organization, laboratory set-up and clean-up, inventory, and laundry. 2. Provide academic support to first-year students as requested by faculty. 3. Assist faculty with administrative tasks, grading, and other responsibilities as assigned. Required Qualifications Enrollment as a second-year student in the Gannon University Doctor of Physical Therapy Program. Successful completion of cadaver-based anatomy course Demonstrate professionalism, dependability, and organizational skills. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Ability to work collaboratively as part of the Graduate Assistant team and contribute to shared program responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications No instances of academic or professional behavior probation. Physical Demands Fall Semester: Work is performed primarily in the human gross anatomy laboratory. Responsibilities require standing for extended periods, performing fine motor tasks associated with cadaver dissection, and adhering to laboratory safety protocols, including the use of required personal protective equipment. Graduate Assistants must be comfortable working in a cadaver laboratory and around chemical preservatives. Spring Semester: Work is performed primarily in physical therapy teaching laboratories, classrooms, and office settings. Responsibilities require standing for extended periods, assisting with routine laboratory set-up and organization, and using standard instructional and office equipment. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Lab Assistant/Tutoring) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15198": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant for University Well-being",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant for University Well-being Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant for University Well-being Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please email Nora McCann at mccann010@gannon.edu for more information regarding the position. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant for University Well-being Posting Number AS1091P Subdivision Recreation & Wellness Division Student Development & Engagemt Department Wellness Program Location Erie, Pa Position Summary POSITION SUMMARY Under the supervision of the Well-being Director, the Graduate Assistant (GA) for University Well-being assists in the management of wellness programs and campaigns in collaboration with campus and community partners. Responsibilities include: planning and implementing physical activity and nutrition challenges, and coordinating well-being related programming. These programs include Gannon Moves, Wellness Adventure Week Activities, active work stations, ergonomics programming, Stress Less Week, and Type 2 Could Be You, and Summer CSA Programming. The Well-being Graduate Assistant also supports operations related to signature events on campus and in the community such as Step it Up Erie County, West BayFit, Well360 Rewards, Second Harvest Proxy Program, the Wellness Write-in, Hunger-Free Campus Programming, and Tobacco-Free Campus Programming. The GA for University Well-being is part of a larger team and will also have the responsibility of mentoring well-being student staff with assigned projects. The GA must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission and philosophy of well-being. NACE Competencies for Well-being Graduate Assistant: Critical Thinking The Well-being GA is expected to plan and implement wellness programming across the university and community. We strive to proactively anticipate the needs of our participants to provide the best experience possible. Quick decision making and multitasking are essential to provide seamless programming. They must also be able to evaluate the effectiveness of programming and pivot to best fit the needs of our Gannon community. Professionalism The Well-being GA assists with programming for students, staff, faculty and community members. It is essential that they are dependable and professional when they represent the university. Marketing materials that are distributed need to be polished and error free. The GA is responsible for designing and distributing most marketing material to help promote our programming. The GA is expected to attend all wellness events prepared and ready to engage with participants. The Well-being Department works closely as a team and relies on the dependability of our workers to execute programming. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s Degree in Applied Exercise Science, Public Health, Business, or Recreation and Sports Management or health related field. Experience: A minimum of one year experience in wellness, recreation, or fitness center programming, operations, and supervision is preferred. Skills: Must have strong leadership and organizational skills. This individual must be able to work with a diverse population that would include students, faculty, staff, alumni and community leaders. Licenses or Certifications: CPR and First Aid University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a facility and programming. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Administrative) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 10M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule TBD Shift Rotating Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14895": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Cyber System Administrator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Cyber System Administrator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Cyber System Administrator Posting Number AS1124P Subdivision School of Engineering and Computing Division Col. of Engineering & Business Department Cybersecurity Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Cyber System Administrator Position provides operational and technical support for computing systems, instructional spaces, and related academic activities located in the Institute for Health and Cyber Knowledge (I-Hack). This position recommends any procedural changes that would enhance course delivery and academic projects, assists the academic leadership to ensure that established priorities are followed, manages High-Performance Computing Center ( HPC ), and supports the Center for Manufacturing and Technology ( CMT ). He/she has responsibility for the design, implementation, configuration, and management of physical and virtual enterprise server and storage systems and for providing primary support for the network management systems and network operating systems for the cybersecurity programs, HPC , and CMT . He/she will manage many aspects of network and system operations, prevent security incidents, plan for upgrades, and respond to issues that arise. Required Qualifications ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : Administers core systems, Active Directory, Microsoft SQL , cloud computing, patch management, etc., in conjunction with other team members. Administers network security infrastructure. Maintains firewall rules, NAT policies, and access control lists. Manages the student lab environment lifecycle each semester: deploys and configures course VM environments from approved templates, supports classroom workstation imaging and software deployment, and decommissions student resources at semester end. Manages external cloud services. Maintains external service subscriptions and coordinates renewals. Administrates backup infrastructure, defines and maintains backup schedules and retention policies per system tier, and verifies and tests restore procedures. Performs high-level technical support of all manner of server and computer desktop applications providing advice, training, and assistance and serving as a resource person for the cybersecurity program. Consults with the academic program leadership on hardware acquisitions and recommends configurations that meet program’s standards and reflect current technology. Implements and/or provides leadership and guidance for major projects Creates and maintains system documentation, operational procedures, architectural documentation, and hardware/software inventory. Collaborates with institutional IT personnel. Ensures alignment between systems and infrastructure managed in this position with institutional IT commitments. Proposes and implements enhancements that will improve the performance and reliability of all systems and services following industry best practices. Develops, recommends, and implements network standards and policies; monitors compliance with established standards. Assists in evaluating, recommending, and purchasing hardware, software, and services that improve information technology delivery to the program. Maintains and consistently improves their knowledge of emerging technologies. Manages the High-Performance Computing Cluster ( HPC ), including provisioning and maintaining compute resources, virtualized lab environments, and storage capacity to support coursework and faculty needs. Supports hardware and software needs of the cyber faculty and staff in IHack. Coordinate Open House activities and camps as well as support for outreach activities; these include but are not limited to Cyberpatriot, GUBotDev, etc. Support senior design projects. Performs other duties as assigned within the scope and responsibility and requirements of the job. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : The Cyber System Administrator coordinates work for students’ projects and/or departmental projects. Manages undergraduate and graduate student workers Preferred Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS : Education: Bachelor’s degree in a computer-related field or greater than 5 years of equivalent experience required or relevant certifications in cybersecurity. Experience: 2+ years of experience administering Linux-based server infrastructure in a production environment. Experience with virtualization platforms (Proxmox, VMware, or equivalent), network administration, and enterprise storage systems preferred. Experience in an academic or research computing environment is a plus. Technical Skills: Experience administering production data networks, to include switches, routers, firewalls, physical and virtual systems, Proxmox VE (hypervisor cluster management), Ceph distributed storage, OPNsense or pfSense firewall administration, OpenVPN/Wireguard VPN administration, Linux container administration ( LXC /Docker), Authentik or equivalent SSO /identity provider, Nginx/reverse proxy administration, Cloudflare or equivalent CDN / DNS management, infrastructure as code or automation (Ansible, shell scripting, Python), Windows domain, Active directory, and SQL . Working knowledge and experience of TCP /IP, DNS , DHCP , 802.11 technologies, Windows Server Operating systems, Linux Operating Systems, and Cloud computing. Experience installing and supporting client, server, and web applications in a networked physical and virtual environment. Experience with network and server management and analysis tools (hardware and software). Ability to understand the principles of new technologies and products. General Skills: Ability to work independently with minimal supervision; excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal skills; ability to communicate clearly with individual computing users on all levels in small groups, one on one, and in writing; proven experience as a problem solver; proven experience in co-operative teamwork; skill in organizing materials; must be able to oversee an inventory and keep records; project management experience helpful; experience in an academic environment preferred. Licenses and Certifications: CompTIA Security+, Linux+/ LPIC , Microsoft, Networking, and/or cybersecurity certification preferred Interpersonal Skills: General skills include the ability to communicate effectively and professionally, familiarity with organizational issues, and technical expertise. Required to adapt to new computing environments and situations and be alert to new problem areas and will propose possible solutions. Must be adept at pursuing problems until solved through defined channels. Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS : Ability to lift up to 20 pounds. Ability to reach with hands and arms; bend, kneel, crouch and climb ladders. WORKING CONDITIONS : Work is performed in a busy office and University setting. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Technician Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule M-F Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
