    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15224": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | ESE Student Research Assistant (Cao)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | ESE Student Research Assistant (Cao) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help ESE Student Research Assistant (Cao) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If you have any questions about this position, please contact Dr. Liu Cao at cao003@gannon.edu.. Position Details Position Summary Position Title ESE Student Research Assistant (Cao) Posting Number Division School of Engineering and Computing Department Col. of Engineering & Business Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Critical Thinking -The student will gather and analyze the information from the literature and identify the proper solution to the existing problems. It is expected that the student worker will summarize and interpret experimental data, and also prioritize the action steps. Communication -Clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives with persons inside and outside of an organization. Teamwork -Build and maintain collaborative relationships to work effectively toward common goals, while appreciating diverse viewpoints and shared responsibilities. This position provides teaching, laboratory and research support to Dr. Liu Cao in the Environmental Science & Engineering department. Students may help with lab preparation, teaching, and multiple research projects with Dr. Cao assisting in tasks including field sample collection, laboratory processing of samples, water quality analysis, air quality analysis, chemical and biological analysis if environmental samples, data management and analysis. Students are strongly encouraged to reach out to Dr. Cao (cao003@gannon.edu) first to talk about research interest before applying to this position. Required Qualifications Full-time undergraduate student majoring in environmental science, environmental engineering, or students who took college-level chemistry courses. Ability to multitask and work independently. Good organizational skills and reliability. Good academic standing at the university. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands This position requires minimal physical demands, but applicants should be able to safely lift 40 pounds and sit and/or stand for extended periods. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Job Posting Open Date 09/01/2026 Job Posting Close Date 09/09/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants If you have any questions about this position, please contact Dr. Liu Cao at cao003@gannon.edu.. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
