    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15051": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant (Tutoring and Lab Assistants); Tutor 2nd Year focus/Social Media FA26",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant (Tutoring and Lab Assistants); Tutor 2nd Year focus/Social Media FA26 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant (Tutoring and Lab Assistants); Tutor 2nd Year focus/Social Media FA26 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant (Tutoring and Lab Assistants); Tutor 2nd Year focus/Social Media FA26 Posting Number AS1157P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Physical Therapy Program Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The physical therapy program at Gannon University is committed to excellence in student-centered learning, with an emphasis on student-learning outcomes. Our graduate assistants play an important role in achieving these outcomes, working collaboratively with program faculty and colleagues as they assist in program operations, hosting open-lab times with first year students, tutoring as requested by the faculty, and in practice opportunities. Graduate assistants must maintain student confidentiality, display initiative, and be flexible with work requirements. This position is for students entering the third year of the DPT program . This position will be remote after fall break and follows the university academic calendar. Career Readiness Competencies Technology: Utilize social media effectively and ethically to support the needs of the program. Teamwork: Collaborate with faculty and fellow Graduate Assistants to support program operations, assist one another as needed, and contribute to shared program goals. Professionalism: Demonstrate initiative, flexibility, dependability, confidentiality, and timely completion of responsibilities while serving as a leader and representative of the DPT Program. Responsibilities 1. Academic Support Facilitate weekly review sessions for first- and second-year DPT students, including in-person and virtual didactic support as appropriate throughout the academic year. Provide individualized tutoring for first- and second-year students as requested by faculty. Communicate attendance, participation, and session summaries to faculty. Assist faculty with grading and course support as assigned. 2. Communications and Marketing Manage the DPT Program’s social media platforms and develop content that highlights student, faculty, and program accomplishments. Develop and distribute program newsletters and other marketing materials. Maintain and update program pages, Blackboard resources, scholarship information, and other student-facing communications. 3. Program Operations Assist with the organization and preparation of instructional spaces, laboratory activities, and other program initiatives as assigned. Maintain Graduate Assistant time records and other program documentation. Support student engagement initiatives, including Wellness Wednesdays and Community Health Initiative ( CHI ) activities. Perform additional administrative and program support responsibilities as assigned by faculty. Required Qualifications Enrollment as a second-year student in the Gannon University Doctor of Physical Therapy Program. Demonstrated academic success and strong foundational knowledge appropriate to providing peer academic support. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated professionalism, dependability, initiative, and organizational skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, fellow Graduate Assistants, and students. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Proficiency with common technology platforms, including Microsoft Office, Blackboard, and social media, or the ability to learn new technologies as needed. Preferred Qualifications No instances of academic or professional behavior probation. Experience in copywriting, public relations, or social media/marketing preferred. Physical Demands Responsibilities are performed primarily in classroom, laboratory, and office settings. Duties require standing or walking for extended periods during review sessions and program activities, routine use of computers and other instructional technology, and occasional set-up and organization of instructional spaces and materials. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Lab Assistant/Tutoring) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
