    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15173": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | GO College Middle School Tutor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help GO College Middle School Tutor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Be sure to include updated resume. Position Details Position Summary Position Title GO College Middle School Tutor Posting Number Division Dean's Office; CHES Department Col.Humanities,Ed.&SocScience Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Career and Self-Development - tutor will develop more skills/awareness by working with students who are exploring their own career pathways and life skills. Leadership - tutors will lead students through workshop teaching materials, personal advising, and event management. Equity and Inclusion – by working with students, tutors will become more aware of the high needs of our students. Teamwork - GO College staff works as a team continuously in the office and during events. Communication - GO College tutors learn to diversify their communication styles to effectively impact our students. Gannon University’s GO College program is seeking tutors/mentors to work at Strong Vincent Middle School for after school tutoring, field trip chaperones, and mentoring. GO College is a federally & locally funded college access program that provides free tutoring, mentoring, field trips (campus and career focused) and academic advising for 6th through 8th graders. Required Qualifications Ability to obtain clearances (criminal, FBI , child-abuse). Must be well-rounded academically, but the ability to tutor in math and science is essential. *Outgoing personality and ability to work with a variety of personalities, cultures, and learning abilities Preferred Qualifications Previous experience tutoring/mentoring in a middle school and/or high school. Availability from 2:45-4:00 PM on both Monday and Wednesday Availability during normal school hours for workshop planning and office work. Must be able to tutor all subjects, but most predominantly math and science. *Must be able to commute to Strong Vincent Middle School. Physical Demands N/A Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 4 Job Posting Open Date 08/27/2026 Job Posting Close Date 10/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Be sure to include updated resume. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
