    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15226": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant, Speech Language Pathology Program-Erie, PA",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant, Speech Language Pathology Program-Erie, PA Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant, Speech Language Pathology Program-Erie, PA Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit a letter of interest describing experience to be successful in this role, in addition to technology expertise and email Dr. Hill at hill059@gannon.edu to express interest. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant, Speech Language Pathology Program-Erie, PA Posting Number AS1149P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Speech-Language Pathology Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Communication – Clearly and effectively exchange oral and written exchange of information, ideas, facts, and perspectives with others inside and outside of the organization. Critical Thinking – Identify and respond to the needs department and program needs based upon an understanding of situational context and analysis of relevant information. Professionalism – Understand and demonstrate effective work habits and act in the interest of the larger workplace and community. Technology – Understand and leverage technologies ethically to enhance efficiencies, complete tasks, and accomplish goals. The CSD Department and MS- SLP program seek a graduate assistant who will be proactive and positive in meeting established goals and deadlines in the following activities: Assist in creating the monthly newsletter, faculty updates, and announcements including the creation of resources/templates/displays for program promotion and operation. Assist with recruitment and retention initiatives, including assisting with management of social media and community outreach, and coordinating with NSSLHA and interested student volunteers. Organization and inventory management of department/program resources and materials. Assist with scheduling and organization of department, program and clinic meetings. *Other duties, based on needs assigned by Chair/Program Director and Coordinator of Clinical Education. Required Qualifications *Must be enrolled in the first year of the Gannon University Master of Science in Speech-Language Pathology program in Erie, Pennsylvania. *Must have demonstrated academic excellence as an undergraduate student with a cumulative GPA of 3.2 or higher on a 4.0 scale. *Must demonstrate strong time-management, organizational skills, and written and verbal communication skills. *Must be proficient in or comfortable learning and using a variety of software applications, including Microsoft Excel, Microsoft Office Suite, Canva, and other cloud-based productivity and collaboration tools . *Must be able to work independently while also collaborating effectively with faculty, staff, clinic patients and families, and fellow graduate students. *Must demonstrate professionalism, attention to detail, reliability, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities while meeting deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Applicants may distinguish themselves through experiences and personal qualities that demonstrate their potential for success in a rigorous graduate program and the speech-language pathology profession. Examples include a positive and growth-oriented attitude, effective teamwork and collaboration skills, a demonstrated history of volunteerism or community service, leadership experiences, strong communication and interpersonal skills, cultural responsiveness, professionalism, resilience, and a commitment to serving individuals with communication and swallowing disorders. These experiences and attributes may provide applicants with a competitive advantage during the holistic admissions review process. Physical Demands Lift 20 lbs. or less. Function in a busy office environment. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Support Office Position Type GA (Administrative) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 10M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Flexible within class schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
