    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15202": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant - Strategic Communication",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant - Strategic Communication Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant - Strategic Communication Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit resume and cover letter with application. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant - Strategic Communication Posting Number AS1162P Subdivision School of Communication & the Arts Division Col.Humanities,Ed.&SocScience Department Health Communications Location Erie, Pa Position Summary This is a professional position in which the graduate assistant will engage in work that will not only benefit the program and school but will also provide the individual with valuable work experience. Responsibilities of the graduate assistant include: • Assisting faculty or adjuncts in the classroom as needed. • Working with faculty on research projects. • Working on external projects for community partners. • Assisting with social media efforts for the School of Communication and the Arts. • Planning and executing internal and external events. • Assisting with various school and programmatic duties. The position responsibilities vary daily and depend on the needs of the faculty in the department. Career Readiness Learning Objectives : Career and Self-Development – The student will learn to work independently on projects and will be expected to take initiative and ownership of projects and tasks. Teamwork – The student will work closely with the faculty and staff in the School of Communication and the Arts to complete projects and plan and execute events. Communication – The student assistant will create social media content to communicate with internal and external audiences. Professionalism – The student will be responsible for maintaining a regular work schedule and representing the department as needed. Required Qualifications Graduate assistants must be students in the MA in Strategic Communication program. The GA must demonstrate strong communication skills including the ability to: • Work in a classroom. • Manage social media accounts. • Work in a busy office environment. Preferred Qualifications Previous research experience is beneficial. Physical Demands Demands consistent with a typical office position. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Administrative) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14833": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Assistant or Associate Professor and Program Director of Clinical Mental Health Counseling",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assistant or Associate Professor and Program Director of Clinical Mental Health Counseling Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant or Associate Professor and Program Director of Clinical Mental Health Counseling Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor and Program Director of Clinical Mental Health Counseling Posting Number F249P Division Dept. of Psychology & Counseling Department Col.Humanities,Ed.&SocScience Location Ruskin, Fl Position Summary The Gannon University College of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences (Ruskin, Florida Campus) invites applications for a full-time, 12-month tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor and Program Director of Clinical Mental Health Counseling. The Program Director will have teaching and advising responsibilities and will be provided release time for administrative duties. Candidates must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its liberal arts and professional education traditions. Gannon University has CACREP accredited Clinical Mental Health Counseling programs at the Erie and Ursuline College campuses, both of which are in high demand and currently at enrollment capacity. The Program Director is responsible for developing curriculum for a new program in Ruskin, Florida and developing initial relationships with clinical placement sites. With support from colleagues at the other two Gannon University campuses, the Program Director will prepare the new program to comply with accreditation standards as a secondary location, with a goal of admitting a first cohort of students in Fall 2028. Upon launch of the new program, the successful candidate will engage in student recruitment, teach graduate courses, advise students, and participate in departmental, college, and university committees and service activities. The program director will be responsible for assessment, budget management, CACREP reporting, and participate in recruitment of additional faculty. Ideal candidates will provide evidence of competence in interactive and collaborative teaching styles, as well as active scholarship in the counseling field and commitment to teaching in a liberal arts setting. Qualified candidates will be expected to work collaboratively with colleagues, advise students and prepare them intellectually, professionally, and personally, and engage in scholarly activities in keeping with the Boyer Model of Scholarship as is appropriate to the application and receipt of tenure and promotion at Gannon. Requirements include an earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision (completed by time of appointment) with demonstrated teaching excellence in higher education. Licensure as a Professional Counselor, or ability to obtain licensure in Florida within one year of hire, is preferred. Qualified candidates will be proficient in curriculum design, program administration, program evaluation, instruction and advising, and knowledgeable about CACREP accreditation requirements and process. Gannon University is a Catholic, Diocesan university dedicated to excellence in teaching, scholarship and service. Our faculty and staff prepare students to be global citizens through programs grounded in the liberal arts and sciences and professional specializations. Inspired by the Catholic Intellectual Tradition, we offer a comprehensive, values-centered learning experience that emphasizes faith, leadership, inclusiveness and social responsibility. Located along Florida’s stunning Gulf Coast, the town of Ruskin is a relaxed community conveniently nestled within the bustling Tampa Bay area, with close proximity to St. Petersburg. Gannon University seeks excellence through inclusiveness and invites members of underrepresented groups to apply. Gannon University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For more information about Gannon visit www.gannon.edu. Application Procedure: Submit a cover letter, CV, and the contact information for three professional references to https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/. Review of applications will begin immediately and this position will remain open until filled. The finalist will be required to submit an original transcript from the institution awarding their terminal degree. References will not be contacted without permission from applicants. Required Qualifications Education: An earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision (completed by time of appointment) with demonstrated teaching excellence in higher education. Rank: In accordance with the University’s standards, Provost and Vice President for Student Experience awards initial rank at the time of employment. Licenses and Certifications: Licensure as a Professional Counselor, or ability to obtain licensure in Florida within one year of hire, is preferred. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s inclusive Mission, its Catholic identity, and its strong liberal arts foundation that supports exemplary professional education programs. Preferred Qualifications Qualified candidates will be proficient in curriculum design, program administration, program evaluation, instruction and advising, and knowledgeable about CACREP accreditation requirements and process. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy academic environment and necessary travel. Work is performed in a busy classroom and office setting. Tenure Status Tenure Track Position Type Regular Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Credits Per Year 24 credits Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
