      "title": "Gannon University  | Assistant Men&#39;s &amp; Women&#39;s Water Polo Coach",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assistant Men&#39;s &amp; Women&#39;s Water Polo Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Men's & Women's Water Polo Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Men's & Women's Water Polo Coach Posting Number AS1085P Subdivision Athletic Director's Office Division Athletics Department Athletics Location Erie, Pa Position Summary This position assists the Head Men’s and Women’s Water Polo Coach during practices and games (at least 60%); assists with various tasks associated with recruiting while adhering to the WWPA and NCAA regulations. In addition, assists with equipment management and general record keeping. Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. 1. Assists head coach with team training and various administrative responsibilities including, but not limited to, fundraising, community service, and recruiting. 2. Assists with monitoring study tables. 3. Assists with various practice and game-related duties. 4. Understands and complies with all NCAA and Gannon University regulations. 5. Assists in the development and implementation of camps and clinics. 6. Performs other duties as assigned within the scope and responsibility and requirements of the job. Required Qualifications Must have excellent written and verbal communication skills; demonstrated organizational and time management skills; and the ability to effectively assist with teaching and coaching swimming and water polo skills and strategy. Must have prior playing or coaching experience, preferably at the college level. Must have a valid driver’s license in good standing. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with coaching an intercollegiate athletic team. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 10M Hours per Week varies Work Schedule varies Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). I attest that I have not been suspended from coaching by another NCAA member institution. Yes No Have you been prohibited from certain coaching-related activities as a result of violations while employed by another NCAA member institution? Yes No Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
