    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14835": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Assistant Coach, Women&#39;s Lacrosse",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assistant Coach, Women&#39;s Lacrosse Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Coach, Women's Lacrosse Posting Number AS1141P Subdivision Athletic Director's Office Division Athletics Department Athletics Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Assistant Coach for Women’s Lacrosse is a full-time, twelve-month position and is responsible for assisting the Head Coach in all aspects of the Women’s Lacrosse program. The program competes in the Pennsylvania State Athletic Association ( PSAC ) at the NCAA Division II level. Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : 1. Recruits quality academic students who are also competitive student-athletes. 2. Trains, strengthens, and develops all student-athletes on a year-round schedule, under the direction of the Head Coach. 3. Learns, understands, and complies with all PSAC , NCAA , and Gannon University regulations. 4. Promotes and represents the University whenever possible. 5. Assists in the development and implementation of a year-round strength and conditioning program for the team. 6. Assists with the overall recruiting process, including on and off-campus recruiting activities and events. 7. Assists with scouting, film upload and exchange, game planning, and game day strategies. 8. Assists in the development and implementation of camps and clinics. 9. Performs other duties as assigned within the scope and responsibility and requirements of the job. Required Qualifications Education: A bachelor’s degree; working knowledge of PSAC and NCAA regulations. Must be able to pass the NCAA recruiting/education modules annually. Experience: Collegiate coaching or playing experience, with an ability to recruit. Skills: Must have excellent written and verbal communication skills; demonstrated organizational and time management skills; and the ability to effectively teach and coach lacrosse skills and strategy. Certifications and Licenses: A valid driver’s license that is in good standing is required. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with an intercollegiate athletic team. Work is performed in a busy office, outdoor field instruction, and University setting. Travel is required. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week varies Work Schedule varies Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * I attest that I have not been suspended from coaching by another NCAA member institution. Yes No * Have you been prohibited from certain coaching-related activities as a result of violations while employed by another NCAA member institution? Yes No Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
