    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15180": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | BIOL 366 HGAL Student Worker Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help BIOL 366 HGAL Student Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please Note: If you haven’t been previously contacted by the Biology Department Chairperson / Human Gross Anatomy lab coordinator, this position is NOT for you. Position Details Position Summary Position Title BIOL 366 HGAL Student Worker Posting Number Division School of Sciences Department Col.Health Professions & Sci. Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Biology Department is looking for eight (8) student workers in the Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters for BIOL 366 Human Gross Anatomy Laboratory course. The laboratory-teaching assistant student worker must be an undergraduate student currently enrolled in biology major or related majors/programs at Gannon University. The laboratory-teaching assistant will be responsible for assisting lab instructors in performing teaching or teaching-related duties in BIOL 366. Primary responsibilities include: 1. Dissection of human cadavers, from head to toe and from skin to bone, as well as preparation of human cadavers for dissection at the start of the semester. 2. Help instructors set up, proctor, and grade lab practical exams and a lab practical exam during finals week (typically on Thursday of finals week). 3. Follow all safety guidelines at all times in the laboratory, and instruct and enforce these guidelines for all students in the laboratory. 4. Promptly relay any problems encountered with the laboratory sessions to the supervising faculty member, and report equipment maintenance or room maintenance problems to the supervising faculty member. 5. Set up equipment and specimens before each laboratory session. 6. Be available and professional to students during official laboratory periods and be prepared to help students with questions during the laboratory period. 7. Lead one or two open lab and dissection lab sections per week. Be available and professional to students during these sessions and be prepared to help students with questions during these sessions. 8. Properly package human material into biohazard bags and prepare the dissected cadavers for transport at the end of the finals week each semester. 8. Clearly and fully understand the material to be covered in the lab session, how to handle it in the laboratory, and how it is related to the lectures. 9. Attend meetings scheduled by the supervising faculty member. 10. Clean up the laboratory at the end of each session. 11. Complete time entry online biweekly before the deadline. The pay rate of this position is $10.00/hour, up to 5-7 hours/week during the Fall and Spring semesters. Required Qualifications 1. Must have earned at least a grade of B+ in both BIOL 365 and BIOL 366 courses. 2. Must be willing to work on the weekends during the semester and during finals week. Please Note: If you haven’t been previously contacted by the Biology Department Chairperson / Human Gross Anatomy lab coordinator, this position is NOT for you. Preferred Qualifications 1. Excellent oral communication skills 2. A willingness to explain anatomical structures and concepts to other undergraduate students. 3. Willing to work as part of an instructional team. Physical Demands 1. Moving, positioning, and adjusting both human cadavers, and the tanks in which the cadavers are stored. 2. Standing and bending for prolonged period as per the requirement of the dissection of the cadavers 3. Lifting and moving the organ storage bins 4. Ability to climb a ladder and carry heavy models. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 8 Job Posting Open Date 08/28/2026 Job Posting Close Date 09/07/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please Note: If you haven’t been previously contacted by the Biology Department Chairperson / Human Gross Anatomy lab coordinator, this position is NOT for you. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14498": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Assistant Women&#39;s Wrestling Coach",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assistant Women&#39;s Wrestling Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach Posting Number AS1078P Subdivision Athletic Director's Office Division Athletics Department Athletics Location Erie, Pa Position Summary POSITION SUMMARY : The Assistant Women’s Wrestling Coach is a full-time, 12-month position. The position is responsible for assisting the Head Women’s Wrestling Coach in all aspects of the Women’s Wrestling program, ensuring adherence to NCAA compliance. Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : 1. Assists with recruiting student-athletes that are committed to academic and athletic excellence. 2. Has adequate training and background to properly plan, implement, train, and coach women’s wrestling at the collegiate level. 3. Assists Head Coach with team training and various administrative responsibilities, including but not limited to, community service, academic support, fundraising, and recruiting. 4. Learns, understands, and complies with all NCAA and Gannon University policies and requirements. 5. Promotes a positive student-athlete experience. 6. Promotes and represents the University whenever possible. 7. Assists with the design and development of strength and conditioning plans. 8. Assists with the operation and instruction of camps and clinics. 9. Demonstrates effective communication and collaboration skills within the program, department, and University. 10. Performs other duties as assigned within the scope and responsibility and requirements of the position. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS : Education: A Bachelor’s Degree; working knowledge of freestyle wrestling techniques and NCAA rules and an understanding of the philosophy behind them. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Experience: Freestyle wrestling experience. Women’s wrestling coaching and/or competitive experience at the collegiate level is strongly preferred. Licensure: Must have a valid driver’s license in good standing and CPR / AED and First Aid certified. Skills: Must have excellent written and verbal communication skills; demonstrated organizational and time management skills; technical knowledge of freestyle wrestling skills and strategy combined with the ability to effectively teach and coach them; the ability to motivate and effectively communicate with student-athletes; strong administrative skills such as prioritization, organization, and budgeting; ability to work independently and to work under pressure. Preferred Qualifications Prior collegiate competitive and/or coaching experience. Certified strength and conditioning coach. Physical Demands PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS : Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with a busy athletic team schedule. WORKING CONDITIONS : Work is performed indoors and outdoors in a busy University setting. The work schedule will vary with heavier emphasis September through May. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week varies Work Schedule varies Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * I attest that I have not been suspended from coaching by another NCAA member institution. Yes No * Have you been prohibited from certain coaching-related activities as a result of violations while employed by another NCAA member institution? Yes No Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
