    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15206": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | School of Education Graduate Assistant (Administrative)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | School of Education Graduate Assistant (Administrative) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help School of Education Graduate Assistant (Administrative) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title School of Education Graduate Assistant (Administrative) Posting Number AS1135P Subdivision School of Education Division Col.Humanities,Ed.&SocScience Department Education Program Location Erie, Pa Position Summary CAREER READINESS LEARNING OBJECTIVES : Career & Self Development: This position will help students to identify their strengths and weaknesses within the workplace. Once identified, students can develop a plan of continual personal growth and professional learning while learning to how to navigate their future career path. Professionalism: This position will help prepare students for their future careers by developing effective work habits, learning how to prioritize objectives, and learning how to communicate effectively with others. Students will also learn the importance of attention to detail, dependability, accountability, and being prepared The Graduate Assistant for the School of Education will be assisting the faculty and administrative staff within the department. Duties may include but are not limited to general office work (e.g. filing, printing, scanning, campus deliveries, organization, inventory), general research (e.g. best practices and programs, comparison and review of peer institutions, research new ideas/concepts, etc.), or any special projects associated with the college. DAILY DUTIES : 1. Restock copy machine. 2. Serve as SOE receptionist. 3. Maintain the job bulletin board. 4. Upkeep of SOE social media platforms. 5. Student file maintenance, organization, and filing. 6. Sort mail into the correct mailboxes in the faculty room. 7. Make sure that all areas of the SOE are always clean and neat. 8. Prepare daily course materials for faculty and staff such as copies. 9. Greet students and visitors and direct them to the appropriate office As a student representative of Gannon University and the School of Education, the utmost professionalism and integrity is expected at all times. Required Qualifications 1. Familiar with utilizing social media platforms. 2. Excellent reading, writing, typing, proofreading, and editing skills. 3. Ability to handle multiple responsibilities as shown by previous work experience. 4. Must be proficient in Adobe, MS Excel, MS Forms, MS PowerPoint, and MS Word. 5. Must be able to maintain strict confidentiality and sign confidentiality agreement. 6. Reliable, honest; must be in good academic standing with no prior academic integrity violations; required to adhere to strict confidentiality policies Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands 1) Should be able to bend, lift, push and pull to assist with moving boxes and supplies in various areas throughout the Palumbo Academic Center. 2) May be asked to lift up to 30-50 pounds. 3) May be asked to transport items across campus. Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Administrative) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 9M Hours per Week 10 Work Schedule Office Hours - Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14854": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Athletics Events and Facilities Assistant",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Athletics Events and Facilities Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Athletics Events and Facilities Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please contact Ed Voll, voll003@gannon.edu, Assistant Director of Athletics for Budget and Planning, with any questions regarding the position or application process. Hiring preference will be given to students who are eligible for Federal Work Study.  If you are hired, your continued employment may be contingent on you remaining eligible for Federal Work Study. Position Details Position Summary Position Title Athletics Events and Facilities Assistant Posting Number Division Athletic Director's Office Department Athletics Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Career Readiness Learning Objectives Communication – The student-worker will enhance their communication skills through interactions with fellow students, coaches, athletic department staff, spectators, and members of the campus community. Teamwork – The student-worker will work in collaboration with other student-workers and athletic department staff towards a common goal. The student-worker will assume shared responsibilities related to their schedule and interests and will work with other team members to ensure that all shifts are covered and that the work is being done at a high level. The Athletics Events and Facilities Assistant is a part-time position and is responsible for assisting the Internal Operations Coordinator and/or the Events and Facilities division. This position will assist with game day operations and supervision in the weight room and equipment room. Essential Functions: 1. Must be able to follow instructions and work independently to achieve outlined goals. 2. Must be able to meet the physical demands of the position and at a minimum lift 30lbs. 3. Work is preformed indoors and outdoors in a busy University Setting. 4. The work schedule will vary depending on the number of events. (Predominantly evening and weekend shifts) 5. Ability to operate a washer and dryer 6. Good interpersonal skills 7. Detail-oriented 8. Responsible for the supervision of the varsity weight room during weekend and open weight room hours. 9. Must be able to follow instruction and work independently to achieve outlined goals. 10. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Must be a current student at Gannon University. Hiring preference will be given to students who are eligible for Federal Work Study.  If you are hired, your continued employment may be contingent on you remaining eligible for Federal Work Study. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands -Must be able to meet the physical demands: -Must be able to lift 30lbs. -Work is performed indoors and outdoors in a busy University setting. The work schedule will vary depending on the number of home events. Predominately evening and weekend responsibilities. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 10 Job Posting Open Date 08/07/2026 Job Posting Close Date 09/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please contact Ed Voll, voll003@gannon.edu, Assistant Director of Athletics for Budget and Planning, with any questions regarding the position or application process. Hiring preference will be given to students who are eligible for Federal Work Study.  If you are hired, your continued employment may be contingent on you remaining eligible for Federal Work Study. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you available to work evenings and weekends? Yes No * Are you eligible for Federal Work Study as determined by the Financial Aid Office? Yes No Unsure Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15123": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | STEM Center - STEM-PASS - Course: PHYS 212 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help STEM Center - STEM-PASS - Course: PHYS 212 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Position Details Position Summary Position Title STEM Center - STEM-PASS - Course: PHYS 212 Posting Number Division Library Department Provost & Student Experience (AA) Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Believe in your potential to help make the challenging possible by fueling confidence Lead a cohesive group learning environment throughout the semester, along the way increasing your capacity for growth in group presentation skills and professional communication Unleash your creative spirit to help students see how the big ideas and little concepts come together in a course you love and value Enjoy observing the countless “aha” moments as students you meet with all semester grow and achieve Key responsibilities and highlights: Both new applicants and returning tutors are encouraged to apply for this role (previous experience is not required) Prepares for and facilitates group study sessions and recitations for students in one instructor’s course This target course is designated by faculty, who must inherently want and plan for STEM - PASS for their course It is preferred for the STEM - PASS tutor to sit in on class regularly to re-experience the material and current student expectations Each target course usually has three sessions per week Some initial and ongoing (paid) training is likely to be required Communicates and meets with faculty as necessary to deliver quality student experience Must be able to attend a weekly team meeting (several different options will be available, and this will be communicated in advance of Advising Day so that those offered this role have opportunity to keep at least one of the meeting times free in their schedules!) This role requires reliability to keep scheduled hours for sessions, and often sitting in on class, but provides flexibility in when and where other (paid) preparation time is spent; it is ideal for primary employment Position Structure: Will facilitate and prepare for 2 one-hour sessions per week Will attend most class times along with students, unless an alternate arrangement is made Will communicate regularly with faculty and STEM Center (director, student managers, and other personnel) Will participate in occasional training sessions Critical Thinking/Problem Solving: A STEM tutor can develop critical thinking and problem-solving skills by breaking down complex concepts for students, identifying gaps in their understanding, and helping them develop strategies to solve problems. Oral/Written Communication: STEM tutors need to clearly explain complex ideas and concepts to students within tutoring sessions and in interactions with coworkers and STEM Center management. Tutors may be required to speak to classes, reach out to students, and represent the STEM Center at functions or events. Additionally, tutors may be required to send emails, make phone calls, or initiate other communication on behalf of the STEM Center. Lead tutors will also communicate more with faculty, staff, and other tutors. Teamwork/Collaboration: STEM tutors can facilitate or assist with group study sessions and participate in other projects or initiatives to support the STEM Center. Lead tutors will need to work independently to meet goals in coordination with STEM Center staff and faculty, and may coordinate the efforts of other tutors in doing so. Digital Technology: Tutors may create online resources, utilizing software or apps to visualize concepts, and must make extensive use of scheduling systems, MS Teams, and other software to perform essential functions of the job. Leadership: In working with a variety of students, tutors have regular opportunity to thrive in changing environments, to identify and address complex problems, and to navigate ambiguity. Professionalism/Work Ethic: By being punctual, prepared, and professional in their interactions with students, tutors can showcase a strong work ethic. They must also adhere to ethical guidelines and respect the confidentiality of their students. Career Management: The STEM Center is a cocurricular opportunity to develop and showcase the ability to build success in others and specifically to teach or train others. Tutoring course material often builds additional competencies in those areas. Global/Intercultural Fluency: To develop global and intercultural fluency, tutors often have opportunities to work with a diverse slate of Gannon students, learning, understanding, and adapting to academic and nonacademic facets of culture and communication. Required Qualifications Academic qualifications to tutor course listed in position title High GPA and positive reputation with faculty Interpersonal excellence Final instructor approval Preferred Qualifications Ability to sit in on class at one of the following times: MWF 11:15 12:10 MWF 12:20 01:15 Physical Demands N/A Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 2 Job Posting Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Have you or will you soon complete the REQUIRED questionnaire at: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV ? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
