    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15189": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Regional Advancement Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Regional Advancement Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please apply with your resume, cover letter, and include three professional references. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Regional Advancement Officer Posting Number AS1125P Subdivision UA VP's Office Division University Advancement Department University Advancement Location Ruskin, Fl Position Summary Regional Advancement Officers at Gannon are key members of the University Advancement team reporting to the Vice President while covering territories and constituent groups associated with one or more campuses. The primary responsibility of this full-time role is to help Gannon meet and exceed fundraising goals through effective identification, qualification, cultivation, and solicitation of donors, and in facilitating planned stewardship activity. Advancement Officers are also reviewed on their ability to work effectively with members of a team and with colleagues and volunteers who support Advancement work. This Regional Advancement Officer will be based at our Ruskin, FL campus and will report to the Vice President in Erie, PA while maintaining a hybrid schedule. 1. Effectively manage a portfolio of philanthropic prospects to secure annual, leadership, major, and deferred gifts in support of attainable yet challenging fundraising and engagement goals. 2. Build and effectively maintain plans related to travel, face-to-face meetings, and event facilitation, working closely with colleagues and volunteers when appropriate. 3. Create written proposals, cases for support, gift agreements, and other materials to engage individuals, foundations, and corporations in support of university priorities. 4. Leverage performance metrics guided by annual and strategic goals and build momentum around regular activity and achievements. 5. Cultivate and steward donor relationships in a way that requires the highest standards of professional conduct and respect to ensure increased philanthropic support and engagement. 6. Support the President’s Office and the President’s Leadership Team by arranging and facilitating constituent meetings and events as needs arise. 7. Perform other duties as assigned within the scope, responsibility and requirements of the position and informed by Gannon’s Mission and shared values. Required Qualifications Education: A bachelor’s degree is required. Experience: Experience in or familiarity with higher education is required. Interpersonal, organizational, technological, and fundraising skills are required. Proficiency with CRM solutions, Microsoft Office, Outlook, and event management and communications software are required. The ability to work effectively and efficiently as a hybrid employee associated with an affiliate campus is essential. Additionally, the ability to partner as an excellent teammate with a sound work ethic and dedication to higher education and Gannon’s Mission is required. Preferred Qualifications Five or more years of experience in fundraising and alumni/donor relations is preferred. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with the responsibilities of this position. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule Monday-Friday.  Frequent out-of-town, overnight travel.  Ability to work nights and weekends as needed to fulfill job responsibilities Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14564": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Assistant Football Coach",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assistant Football Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Football Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Football Coach Posting Number AS1105P Subdivision Men's Athletics Division Athletics Department Football Location Erie, Pa Position Summary This is a part-time 12-month position that assists the head football coach and offensive coordinator in implementing a competitive NCAA Division II football program. The Gannon University Football Team competes at the NCAA Division II level and the Pennsylvania State Athletic Conference ( PSAC ). ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : 1. Coaches skill development of student-athletes. 2. Coordinates and schedules strength training and conditioning for player development. 3. Promotes healthy orientation of student-athletes. 4. Demonstrates a thorough understanding of and accountability to PSAC and NCAA rules and regulations. 5. Demonstrates a commitment to the academic and athletic success of the student-athletes and NCAA compliance with the highest of ethical standards. 6. Scouts and recruits qualified, competitive student-athletes while maintaining a commitment to their academic success. 7. Performs other duties related as assigned within the scope and responsibility, and requirements of the job. Required Qualifications Education: A bachelor’s degree is required; a master’s degree is desirable. Experience: Applicants must have football coaching or college playing experience. Applicants must possess effective communication skills and the demonstrated ability to work with a diverse population Licenses and Certifications: A valid driver’s license in good standing. Per Gannon’s Institutional Policy Manual there can be no suspensions on the Motor Vehicle Record for 5 years prior to being hired. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Strength and conditioning certified. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with recruiting and coaching a college-level football team. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week varies Work Schedule varies Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * I attest that I have not been suspended from coaching by another NCAA member institution. Yes No * Have you been prohibited from certain coaching-related activities as a result of violations while employed by another NCAA member institution? Yes No Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
