    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15208": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant, PA Program - Ruskin (Tutoring)",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Graduate Assistant, PA Program - Ruskin (Tutoring) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant, PA Program - Ruskin (Tutoring) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We are accepting applications only from current Physician Assistant students in the Class of 2027 at the Ruskin, Florida, location. Please provide at least two letters of recommendation from current PA-Ruskin faculty. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Graduate Assistant, PA Program - Ruskin (Tutoring) Posting Number AS1108P Subdivision School of Health Professions Division Col.Health Professions & Sci. Department Physician Assistant Prgm-Ruskn Location Ruskin, Fl Position Summary This individual provides tutoring opportunities to the didactic year students at the Ruskin, FL, location via Teams and/or Zoom virtual meetings; this tutoring is done in conjunction with and advisement by the PA faculty and adjunct(s). Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Communication and Critical Thinking – This GA will effectively supplement the students’ prior classroom instruction by clarifying and explaining material and, in identifying the students’ needs, will determine the methods to achieve deeper learning and retention by the students who are being tutored. Equity & Inclusion - This GA will demonstrate the awareness, attitude, knowledge, and skills required to equitably engage and include each of the students being tutored, understanding that they may be of different cultures and that this can impact tutoring and learning. • This position runs through the academic year (fall and spring semesters), up to an average of five hours a week, primarily in the evenings in a virtual meetings setting. • Responsibilities include virtual tutoring sessions for the Ruskin PA cohort as well as separate, one-on-one sessions, and communicating the schedule as well as any changes in a timely manner to all; recordkeeping of hours preparing for and actively tutoring, and the students being tutored. • This GA will demonstrate a proactive and positive attitude. • Included in the work hours are regular virtual meetings with one or more of the GA supervisors: the PA Program Director and the Program Secretary. • All GAs must sign a FERPA (Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act) agreement to protect student confidentiality at all times. Required Qualifications This position requires someone who has excellent communication and computer skills and can effectively convey instructional material in tutoring relationships, whether in person or virtually. He or she needs to be highly organized and able to manage tutoring several students at one time. The person in this position has to be comfortable representing Gannon University in a professional way within the organization as well as with other Gannon students. Strong skills of attention to detail, personal initiative, and integrity are a must for this position. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience teaching or mentoring as well as a working knowledge of PowerPoint and Microsoft Teams are desirable. Physical Demands N/A Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type GA (Lab Assistant/Tutoring) Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 10M Hours per Week 5 Work Schedule afternoons/evenings, depending on Candidate's schedule Shift 2nd Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Letter of Recommendation Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Tell us how you maintain constant performance while under time and work load pressures. (Open Ended Question) * Provide examples of how you handled difficult situations with those you have worked with. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience tutoring at the college level or above? Yes No Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14860": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Intramural Sports Referee/Scorekeeper 26-27 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Intramural Sports Referee/Scorekeeper 26-27 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please contact the RWC with any questions regarding this position. Position Details Position Summary Position Title Intramural Sports Referee/Scorekeeper 26-27 Posting Number Division Recreation & Wellness Department Student Development & Engagemt Location Erie, Pa Position Summary POSITION SUMMARY : Career Readiness Learning Objectives: Communication: Clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives withco-workers during games, as well as the players competing in the games. Teamwork: Build and maintain collaborative relationships with co-workers and players to work effectively toward running a smooth game and event. Professionalism: Understanding the difference between a job and social life and having the ability to ref each game fairly and equally. Intramural Sports Official/Scorekeeper is responsible for the safety and maintaining fair play during Intramural Sports activities and events. Officials and Scorekeepers must understand the basic rules of play for applicable sports they are working and must be able to make fair and unbiased judgement through play. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : 1. Responsible for game control of all officiated Intramural Sports activities and events 2. Calling games with honesty and integrity 3. Maintain a professional demeanor at all times 4. Attend required training sessions and demonstrate proficiency in understanding of rules and officiating 5. Enforce established rules during Intramural Sports competition 6. Evaluate and enforce sportsmanship of Intramural Sports teams/participants 7. Ensure a safe environment for Intramural Sports participants by inspecting the playing area before the competition and creating a safe environment for play 8. Apply and assist in first aid, as permitted by any certifications they may personally hold 9. Run captain’s meetings prior to each competition 10. Ensure proper use of all university equipment by program participants 11. Use mature judgment in emergency situations 12. Work special events and promotional opportunities that may take place on evenings, weekends, campus breaks, and across campus 13. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Education: Enrolled full-time student of Gannon University preferably with a minimum of a 2.5 GPA Experience: Experience must include use of Microsoft Word, Excel, and use of standard office equipment such as copy machine, printer, and telephone. Previous customer service, sports, or fitness experience preferred. Certified in First Aid, CPR , and AED Certified preferred. Skills: Leadership skills including strong verbal and written communication skills, working in a team atmosphere, and professionalism. Individual must be able to work with a diverse population that would include students, faculty, staff, alumni and community members. Must be able to work independently without direct supervision on day to day tasks and be able to take initiative. University Mission: Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Ability to lift and carry weight, possibly up to 50lbs unassisted Ability to walk, stand, and move about for approximately 2-8 hours; without access to a chair Ability to stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl Ability to climb (stairs/ladders) or balance Ability to walk around building and potentially across campus Meet the physical demands associated with a busy office and University environment. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies N/A Job Posting Open Date 08/07/2026 Job Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Please contact the RWC with any questions regarding this position. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please list all the sport leagues you would feel comfortable officiating. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15132": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Assistant Director, Donor Relations",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Assistant Director, Donor Relations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director, Donor Relations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please apply with your resume, cover letter, and include three professional references. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Director, Donor Relations Posting Number AS1165P Subdivision UA VP's Office Division University Advancement Department University Advancement Location Erie, Pa Position Summary The Assistant Director for Donor Relations at Gannon is a key member of the University Advancement team reporting to the Director for Constituent Engagement. The primary responsibility of this full-time role is to facilitate planned stewardship and recognition activities that strengthen relationships between the University and its donors. The position plays a central role in demonstrating the impact of philanthropy by connecting donors with students, programs, and outcomes made possible through their support. The Assistant Director is also reviewed on their ability to work effectively with members of a team and with colleagues and volunteers who support the work of Advancement. 1.     Manage stewardship and engagement activities for donor giving societies, including communications, recognition, benefits, special engagement opportunities, and other strategies designed to strengthen donor relationships and encourage continued philanthropic involvement. 2.     Serve as liaison to Financial Aid for donor-funded scholarships. Assist Financial Aid in coordinating annual scholarship awarding and oversee related stewardship processes. Maintain donor and scholarship information, address fund-related questions, and proofread all agreements. 3.     Produce annual endowment report for scholarship and endowment donors. Collaborate within the division, with Finance, Financial Aid, and other partners to gather financial, recipient, programmatic, and impact information to present it in a clear and donor-centered format. 4.     Develop and manage processes that connect scholarship recipients with donors through thank-you letters, videos, testimonials, personal stories, and other expressions of gratitude. Provide students with guidance and resources to help them effectively communicate the impact of donor support. 5.     Develop customized donor impact and stewardship reports for university leadership, fundraising staff, and other colleagues. Gather stories, outcomes, financial information, photographs, testimonials, and related content that demonstrates the impact of significant philanthropic investments. 6.     Coordinate donor recognition efforts across campus, including plaques, signage, donor walls, named spaces, and digital and giving society recognition. Work with Advancement, Marketing & Communications, and others to ensure recognition is accurate, consistent, timely, and aligned with institutional standards and donor agreements. 7.     Maintain donor relationships in a way that requires the highest standards of professional conduct and respect to ensure increased philanthropic support and engagement. 8.     Perform other duties as assigned within the scope, responsibility and requirements of the position and informed by Gannon’s Mission and shared values. Required Qualifications Education: A bachelor’s degree is required. Experience: Two or more years of related experience is required. Experience in fundraising and alumni/donor relations is preferred. Interpersonal, organizational, technological, and excellent customer service skills are required. Proficiency with CRM solutions, Microsoft Office, Outlook, and event management and communications software are required. Additionally, the ability to partner as an excellent teammate with a sound work ethic and dedication to higher education and Gannon’s Mission is required. Preferred Qualifications Experience in fundraising and alumni/donor relations is preferred. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with the responsibilities of this position. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule Monday-Friday is typical, along with the ability to work nights and weekends as needed to fulfill job responsibilities. Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/14691": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | CLEER Docent (Part-Time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help CLEER Docent (Part-Time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary Position Title CLEER Docent (Part-Time) Posting Number AS1129P Subdivision Provost & VP for Student Experience Division Provost & Student Experience (AA) Department Academic Affairs Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Gannon University’s Project NePTWNE is seeking to expand its pool of qualified part-time docents/guides to join the Center for Lake Erie Education and Research ( CLEER ) team. This role is essential for ensuring smooth daily operations including - Welcoming visitors to the open and accessible center space - Assisting visitors with the proper use of interactive exhibit technology within the center - Cleaning touch screens and other exhibit items when not otherwise engaged or as appropriate - Communicating, listening, and sharing thoughts and ideas with visitors based upon interactive exhibits. This position will remain posted for 12 months. Candidates that best fit an open adjunct position, when it come available, will be contacted to determine if they are interested at that time. At the end of 12 months this position will be closed and an new position will be posted if needed. NACE Competencies: Career & Self Development – Worker will gain an awareness of their strengths and weaknesses through active engagement with the public. Communication – Worker will clearly and effectively share information about the proper usage of technology within the center. Critical Thinking – Worker will monitor and respond to needs of visitors to the center based upon situational context and logical analysis. Equity and Inclusion – Worker will work to ensure all people feel welcomed, safe, and included within the center space. Leadership – Worker will employ their strengths to achieve the overall mission of the center. Professionalism – Worker will recognize their role within the public library and act in the interest of Gannon University and the larger community. Teamwork – Worker will work collaboratively, inclusively, and effectively with other team members to create a hospitable work environment and achieve the overall mission of the center. Technology – Worker will clearly and effectively share information about the proper usage of technology within the center. Required Qualifications Willingness to learn about the exhibits Timely and dependable Welcoming and inclusive demeanor Excellent English written and oral skills Preferred Qualifications Multi-lingual BS in environmental science or a related field Physical Demands This position requires minimal physical demands, but applicants should be able to safely lift 25 pounds and sit and/or stand for extended periods of time; be able to work in a busy environment Exempt Status Non-Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Part-Time Position Length 6M Hours per Week 20 Work Schedule Depending On Candidate's Schedule Shift Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15110": {
      "title": "Gannon University",
      "description": "Gannon University  | STEM Center - STEM-PASS - Course: BIOL 368 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help STEM Center - STEM-PASS - Course: BIOL 368 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Position Details Position Summary Position Title STEM Center - STEM-PASS - Course: BIOL 368 Posting Number Division Library Department Provost & Student Experience (AA) Location Erie, Pa Position Summary Believe in your potential to help make the challenging possible by fueling confidence Lead a cohesive group learning environment throughout the semester, along the way increasing your capacity for growth in group presentation skills and professional communication Unleash your creative spirit to help students see how the big ideas and little concepts come together in a course you love and value Enjoy observing the countless “aha” moments as students you meet with all semester grow and achieve Key responsibilities and highlights: Both new applicants and returning tutors are encouraged to apply for this role (previous experience is not required) Prepares for and facilitates group study sessions and recitations for students in one instructor’s course This target course is designated by faculty, who must inherently want and plan for STEM - PASS for their course It is preferred for the STEM - PASS tutor to sit in on class regularly to re-experience the material and current student expectations Each target course usually has three sessions per week Some initial and ongoing (paid) training is likely to be required Communicates and meets with faculty as necessary to deliver quality student experience Must be able to attend a weekly team meeting (several different options will be available, and this will be communicated in advance of Advising Day so that those offered this role have opportunity to keep at least one of the meeting times free in their schedules!) This role requires reliability to keep scheduled hours for sessions, and often sitting in on class, but provides flexibility in when and where other (paid) preparation time is spent; it is ideal for primary employment Position Structure: Will facilitate and prepare for 2 one-hour sessions per week Will attend most class times along with students, unless an alternate arrangement is made Will communicate regularly with faculty and STEM Center (director, student managers, and other personnel) Will participate in occasional training sessions Critical Thinking/Problem Solving: A STEM tutor can develop critical thinking and problem-solving skills by breaking down complex concepts for students, identifying gaps in their understanding, and helping them develop strategies to solve problems. Oral/Written Communication: STEM tutors need to clearly explain complex ideas and concepts to students within tutoring sessions and in interactions with coworkers and STEM Center management. Tutors may be required to speak to classes, reach out to students, and represent the STEM Center at functions or events. Additionally, tutors may be required to send emails, make phone calls, or initiate other communication on behalf of the STEM Center. Lead tutors will also communicate more with faculty, staff, and other tutors. Teamwork/Collaboration: STEM tutors can facilitate or assist with group study sessions and participate in other projects or initiatives to support the STEM Center. Lead tutors will need to work independently to meet goals in coordination with STEM Center staff and faculty, and may coordinate the efforts of other tutors in doing so. Digital Technology: Tutors may create online resources, utilizing software or apps to visualize concepts, and must make extensive use of scheduling systems, MS Teams, and other software to perform essential functions of the job. Leadership: In working with a variety of students, tutors have regular opportunity to thrive in changing environments, to identify and address complex problems, and to navigate ambiguity. Professionalism/Work Ethic: By being punctual, prepared, and professional in their interactions with students, tutors can showcase a strong work ethic. They must also adhere to ethical guidelines and respect the confidentiality of their students. Career Management: The STEM Center is a cocurricular opportunity to develop and showcase the ability to build success in others and specifically to teach or train others. Tutoring course material often builds additional competencies in those areas. Global/Intercultural Fluency: To develop global and intercultural fluency, tutors often have opportunities to work with a diverse slate of Gannon students, learning, understanding, and adapting to academic and nonacademic facets of culture and communication. Required Qualifications Academic qualifications to tutor course listed in position title High GPA and positive reputation with faculty Interpersonal excellence Final instructor approval Preferred Qualifications Ability to sit in on class at one of the following times: MWF 10:10 11:05 MWF 12:20 01:15 Physical Demands N/A Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Job Posting Open Date 08/14/2026 Job Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants In order to be considered, you must fill out supplementary information and upload resume at this Microsoft Forms questionnaire: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV This position carries a Federal Work Study eligible preference, but it is possible that other students can be hired. Previous STEM Center experience and previous STEM Center application is preferred. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Have you or will you soon complete the REQUIRED questionnaire at: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/3LmrskNZYV ? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
