    "https://gannon.peopleadmin.com/postings/15193": {
      "title": "Gannon University  | Coordinator for Grants, Sponsored Programs, and Research",
      "description": "Gannon University  | Coordinator for Grants, Sponsored Programs, and Research Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Log In /Create Account Help Coordinator for Grants, Sponsored Programs, and Research Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please apply with your resume, cover letter, and include three professional references. Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Coordinator for Grants, Sponsored Programs, and Research Posting Number AS1153P Subdivision UA VP's Office Division University Advancement Department University Advancement Location Pepper Pike, OH Position Summary The Coordinator functions as a grant officer and provides assistance in carrying out the mission of the Office of Sponsored Programs and Research ( OSPR ). This position aids in securing external funding opportunities, educating Ursuline College Campus and the Gannon University community about grant procedures, assisting them in the planning, preparation, and submission of grant proposals. The Coordinator supports all phases of grant operations, including clerical and administrative duties. Must be able to support and promote the University’s Mission. Monitor government and foundation websites for funding opportunities. Create and disseminate solicitation summaries to align internal interests with opportunities. Work independently with internal and external stakeholders as part of proposal writing teams. Collaborate with Ursuline College Campus leadership, faculty, and staff regularly. Prepare and submit sponsor forms and lead overall proposal submission to ensure a complete, compliant, and cohesive submission package. Provide grant education and training for faculty/staff through live and/or recorded sessions. Maintain user access and authorization for grant application portals including grants.gov, research.gov, and foundational portal submission sites. Maintain file of institutional documents including, but not limited to, board of trustee list, 501c3 status, indirect cost rate agreements, facilities statements and data management plans. Develop and maintain a grant and report calendar to track and schedule grant proposals, progress reports, and internal and external reports. Provide guidance and follow-up to ensure post-award reporting requirements are met, using the office’s tracking system. Make decisions related to the OSPR in the absence of the Director. Manage office operations and maintains portal site. Perform other duties as assigned within the scope, responsibility and requirements of the position and informed by Gannon’s Mission and shared values. Required Qualifications Education: A bachelor’s degree is required. Experience: Two or more years of grant-related experience. Must possess the following skills: excellent written, verbal, proofreading and organizational skills; the ability to read written instructions and procedure manuals; the ability to enter data into records, logs and websites with accuracy; the ability to prioritize responsibilities, seek direction regarding courses of action; and the ability to research and compile qualitative and quantitative data. The ability to work independently and manage projects. The ability to be effective while reporting to a supervisor and divisional team that are positioned across multiple campuses. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education is preferred. Physical Demands Must be able to meet the physical demands associated with the responsibilities of this position. Exempt Status Exempt Position Classification Professional Position Type Staff Employment Status Full-Time Position Length 12M Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule Monday-Friday.  Ability to work nights and weekends as needed to fulfill job responsibilities. Shift 1st Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Erie, Pennsylvania Campus 109 University Square Erie, Pennsylvania 16541 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 Ruskin, Florida Campus 105 Commercial Center Dr. Ruskin, Florida 33573 1-800-GANNON-U or 814-871-7000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
